			defined by the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act (WIOA), one or more courses or
			classes, or a structured regimen that provides the services in 20 CFR part 680.200 and
			leads to: (a) An industry-recognized certificate or certification, a certificate of
			completion of a registered apprenticeship, a license recognized by the State involved or
			the Federal Government, an associate or baccalaureate degree, or community college
			certificate of completion; (b) Consistent with § 680.350, a secondary school diploma or
			its equivalent; (c) Employment; or (d) Measurable skill gains toward a credential
			described in paragraph (a) or (b) of this section or employment.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "C001942"^^xsd:token ;
