ceds:C000862
  a owl:Class, skos:ConceptScheme ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Rural-Urban Continuum Codes form a classification scheme that distinguishes
			metropolitan (metro) counties by the population size of their metro area, and
			nonmetropolitan (nonmetro) counties by degree of urbanization and adjacency to a metro
			area or areas. The metro and nonmetro categories have been subdivided into three metro
			and six nonmetro groupings, resulting in a nine-part county codification. The codes
			allow researchers working with county data to break such data into finer residential
			groups beyond a simple metro-nonmetro dichotomy, particularly for the analysis of trends
			in nonmetro areas that may be related to degree of rurality and metro proximity.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "C000862"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Economic Research Service Rural-Urban Continuum Code" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf ceds:C000000 ;
  skos:definition """Rural-Urban Continuum Codes form a classification scheme that distinguishes
			metropolitan (metro) counties by the population size of their metro area, and
			nonmetropolitan (nonmetro) counties by degree of urbanization and adjacency to a metro
			area or areas. The metro and nonmetro categories have been subdivided into three metro
			and six nonmetro groupings, resulting in a nine-part county codification. The codes
			allow researchers working with county data to break such data into finer residential
			groups beyond a simple metro-nonmetro dichotomy, particularly for the analysis of trends
			in nonmetro areas that may be related to degree of rurality and metro proximity.""" ;
  skos:notation "ERSRuralUrbanContinuumCode" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Economic Research Service Rural-Urban Continuum Code" .

