ceds:NI001517162963
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Chinese Languages for Native Speakers courses prepare native and heritage speakers to communicate in Chinese languages in all modes. These courses reinforce and expand students' skills to interpret (read, listen, view) and present (speak, write) information at the same level as they exchange (speak and listen; read and write) information, concepts, and ideas on a variety of topics. Chinese Languages for Native Speakers courses advance students' understanding of the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of the cultures included in the Chinese language-speaking world. These courses may be used for any Chinese language, including Mandarin and Cantonese." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517162963"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Chinese Languages for Native Speakers" ;
  skos:definition "Chinese Languages for Native Speakers courses prepare native and heritage speakers to communicate in Chinese languages in all modes. These courses reinforce and expand students' skills to interpret (read, listen, view) and present (speak, write) information at the same level as they exchange (speak and listen; read and write) information, concepts, and ideas on a variety of topics. Chinese Languages for Native Speakers courses advance students' understanding of the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of the cultures included in the Chinese language-speaking world. These courses may be used for any Chinese language, including Mandarin and Cantonese." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "24407" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Chinese Languages for Native Speakers" .

ceds:NI001517162964
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Chinese Languages Field Experience courses place students in environments in
			which they interact with native Chinese languages speakers, typically in settings where
			a Chinese language is the main language spoken. These courses enable students to
			strengthen their skills in exchanging (speaking/listening and writing/reading),
			interpreting (reading, listening, and viewing), and presenting information and their
			ability to interact in culturally appropriate ways. These courses may be used for any
			Chinese language, including Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517162964"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Chinese Languages Field Experience" ;
  skos:definition """Chinese Languages Field Experience courses place students in environments
			in which they interact with native Chinese languages speakers, typically in settings
			where a Chinese language is the main language spoken. These courses enable students to
			strengthen their skills in exchanging (speaking/listening and writing/reading),
			interpreting (reading, listening, and viewing), and presenting information and their
			ability to interact in culturally appropriate ways. These courses may be used for any
			Chinese language, including Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "24408" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Chinese Languages Field Experience" .

ceds:NI001517162965
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB Language A: Language and Literature—Chinese Languages courses prepare
			students to take the International Baccalaureate Language A: Language and Literature
			exams. Course content includes in-depth study of various text types and literary forms,
			composition for purpose and audience, and the context and elements of literature. The
			course includes oral and written assignments and is designed for students highly
			competent in using Chinese languages in an academic context. These courses may be used
			for any Chinese language, including Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517162965"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Language A: Language and Literature—Chinese Languages" ;
  skos:definition """IB Language A: Language and Literature—Chinese Languages courses prepare
			students to take the International Baccalaureate Language A: Language and Literature
			exams. Course content includes in-depth study of various text types and literary forms,
			composition for purpose and audience, and the context and elements of literature. The
			course includes oral and written assignments and is designed for students highly
			competent in using Chinese languages in an academic context. These courses may be used
			for any Chinese language, including Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "24417" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Language A: Language and Literature—Chinese Languages" .

ceds:NI001517162966
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB Language Ab Initio—Chinese Languages courses prepare students to take the
			International Baccalaureate exam. These courses focus on developing the linguistic
			abilities of students with little or no experience with the language of study. Course
			content includes the study of individuals and society, leisure and work, and urban and
			rural environments. These courses also provide students with the opportunity to practice
			and explore this language. These courses may be used for any Chinese language, including
			Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517162966"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Language Ab Initio—Chinese Languages" ;
  skos:definition """IB Language Ab Initio—Chinese Languages courses prepare students to take
			the International Baccalaureate exam. These courses focus on developing the linguistic
			abilities of students with little or no experience with the language of study. Course
			content includes the study of individuals and society, leisure and work, and urban and
			rural environments. These courses also provide students with the opportunity to practice
			and explore this language. These courses may be used for any Chinese language, including
			Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "24418" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Language Ab Initio—Chinese Languages" .

ceds:NI001517162967
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Chinese Languages Conversation and Culture courses provide students with an
			introduction to the Chinese languages and the culture(s) of Chinese language-speaking
			people, placing greater emphasis on speaking and listening skills while deemphasizing
			writing and reading the language. These courses may be used for any Chinese language,
			including Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517162967"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Chinese Languages Conversation and Culture" ;
  skos:definition """Chinese Languages Conversation and Culture courses provide students with an
			introduction to the Chinese languages and the culture(s) of Chinese language-speaking
			people, placing greater emphasis on speaking and listening skills while deemphasizing
			writing and reading the language. These courses may be used for any Chinese language,
			including Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "24409" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Chinese Languages Conversation and Culture" .

ceds:NI001517162968
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Chinese Languages Literature courses prepare students to communicate
			authentically in Chinese languages by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing),
			exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking,
			writing) information, opinions, and ideas drawn from literature written in Chinese
			languages. Emphasis is typically placed on critical and analytical reading and writing,
			understanding the integration of Chinese cultures into literature, and exploring
			interdisciplinary connections. These courses may be used for any Chinese language,
			including Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517162968"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Chinese Languages Literature" ;
  skos:definition """Chinese Languages Literature courses prepare students to communicate
			authentically in Chinese languages by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing),
			exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking,
			writing) information, opinions, and ideas drawn from literature written in Chinese
			languages. Emphasis is typically placed on critical and analytical reading and writing,
			understanding the integration of Chinese cultures into literature, and exploring
			interdisciplinary connections. These courses may be used for any Chinese language,
			including Mandarin and Cantonese.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "24410" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Chinese Languages Literature" .

