ceds:NI001517163305
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level calculus courses, AP Calculus AB provides students with an understanding of the concepts of calculus and experience with its methods and applications. These courses introduce calculus and include the following topics: functions, graphs, limits, and continuity; differential calculus (including definition, application, and computation of the derivative; derivative at a point; derivative as a function; and second derivatives); and integral calculus (including definite integrals and antidifferentiation)." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163305"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Calculus AB" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level calculus courses, AP Calculus AB provides students with an understanding of the concepts of calculus and experience with its methods and applications. These courses introduce calculus and include the following topics: functions, graphs, limits, and continuity; differential calculus (including definition, application, and computation of the derivative; derivative at a point; derivative as a function; and second derivatives); and integral calculus (including definite integrals and antidifferentiation)." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "02124" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Calculus AB" .

ceds:NI001517163611
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Technology/Electronic Music courses emphasize current technology as a means
			to create, record, mix, and otherwise interact with music and music media. These courses
			focus on experimenting with electronic music technology as part of the process for
			creating music.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163611"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Technology/Electronic Music" ;
  skos:definition """Technology/Electronic Music courses emphasize current technology as a means
			to create, record, mix, and otherwise interact with music and music media. These courses
			focus on experimenting with electronic music technology as part of the process for
			creating music.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05124" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Technology/Electronic Music" .

ceds:NI001517163612
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Music (early childhood education) courses provide developmentally
			appropriate activities to enable students to create and perform music, listen and
			respond to musical compositions, and incorporate their musical experiences with other
			activities and subjects. Specific course content conforms to any existing state
			standards for early childhood education.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163612"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Music (early childhood education)" ;
  skos:definition """Music (early childhood education) courses provide developmentally
			appropriate activities to enable students to create and perform music, listen and
			respond to musical compositions, and incorporate their musical experiences with other
			activities and subjects. Specific course content conforms to any existing state
			standards for early childhood education.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05128" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Music (early childhood education)" .

ceds:NI001517163613
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Individual Technique—Instrumental Music courses provide individuals with instruction in instrumental literature and techniques. These courses may be conducted either individually or in a small group; formal and informal performances are typically included as well as experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163613"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Individual Technique—Instrumental Music" ;
  skos:definition "Individual Technique—Instrumental Music courses provide individuals with instruction in instrumental literature and techniques. These courses may be conducted either individually or in a small group; formal and informal performances are typically included as well as experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05109" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Individual Technique—Instrumental Music" .

ceds:NI001517163614
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Chorus courses develop students' vocal skills within the context of a large choral ensemble in which they perform a variety of styles of repertoire. These courses are designed to develop students' vocal techniques and their ability to sing parts and include experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163614"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Chorus" ;
  skos:definition "Chorus courses develop students' vocal skills within the context of a large choral ensemble in which they perform a variety of styles of repertoire. These courses are designed to develop students' vocal techniques and their ability to sing parts and include experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05110" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Chorus" .

ceds:NI001517163615
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Vocal Ensemble courses help students develop vocal techniques and refine their ability to sing parts in small ensembles (e.g., madrigal, barber shop, gospel). Course goals may include helping students develop their solo singing ability and emphasize one or several ensemble literature styles. These ensembles may include both instrumental and vocal music and include experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163615"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Vocal Ensemble" ;
  skos:definition "Vocal Ensemble courses help students develop vocal techniques and refine their ability to sing parts in small ensembles (e.g., madrigal, barber shop, gospel). Course goals may include helping students develop their solo singing ability and emphasize one or several ensemble literature styles. These ensembles may include both instrumental and vocal music and include experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05111" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Vocal Ensemble" .

ceds:NI001517163616
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Individual Technique—Vocal Music courses provide instruction in and encourage the refinement of vocal techniques and repertoire other than the ability to sing in groups. These courses may be conducted individually or in small groups. Formal and informal performances may be part of the instructional program as well as experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163616"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Individual Technique—Vocal Music" ;
  skos:definition "Individual Technique—Vocal Music courses provide instruction in and encourage the refinement of vocal techniques and repertoire other than the ability to sing in groups. These courses may be conducted individually or in small groups. Formal and informal performances may be part of the instructional program as well as experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05112" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Individual Technique—Vocal Music" .

ceds:NI001517163617
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Music Theory courses provide students with an understanding of the
			fundamentals of music and include the following topics: composition, arranging,
			analysis, aural development, and sight reading.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163617"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Music Theory" ;
  skos:definition """Music Theory courses provide students with an understanding of the
			fundamentals of music and include the following topics: composition, arranging,
			analysis, aural development, and sight reading.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05113" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Music Theory" .

ceds:NI001517163618
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "AP Music Theory courses are designed to be the equivalent of a first-year music theory college course as specified by the College Board. AP Music Theory develops students' understanding of musical structure and compositional procedures. Usually intended for students who already possess performance-level skills, AP Music Theory courses extend and build upon students' knowledge of intervals, scales, chords, metric/rhythmic patterns, and the ways they interact in a composition. Musical notation, analysis, composition, and aural skills are important components of the course." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163618"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Music Theory" ;
  skos:definition "AP Music Theory courses are designed to be the equivalent of a first-year music theory college course as specified by the College Board. AP Music Theory develops students' understanding of musical structure and compositional procedures. Usually intended for students who already possess performance-level skills, AP Music Theory courses extend and build upon students' knowledge of intervals, scales, chords, metric/rhythmic patterns, and the ways they interact in a composition. Musical notation, analysis, composition, and aural skills are important components of the course." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05114" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Music Theory" .

ceds:NI001517163619
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "IB Music courses prepare students to take the International Baccalaureate Music exams. IB Music courses develop students' knowledge and understanding of music through study of musical perception, including study of musical elements, form and structure, notations, musical terminology and context. These courses include exploration of music from different places, cultures, and time periods. They also involve training in at least one of the following: creating, solo performing, and group performing." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163619"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Music" ;
  skos:definition "IB Music courses prepare students to take the International Baccalaureate Music exams. IB Music courses develop students' knowledge and understanding of music through study of musical perception, including study of musical elements, form and structure, notations, musical terminology and context. These courses include exploration of music from different places, cultures, and time periods. They also involve training in at least one of the following: creating, solo performing, and group performing." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05115" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Music" .

ceds:NI001517163620
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Music History/Appreciation courses survey different musical styles and periods with the intent of increasing students' understanding of music and its importance in relation to the human experience. Music History/Appreciation courses may focus on how various styles of music apply musical elements to create an expressive or aesthetic impact. Students also have the ability for informal music performance and creation within the classroom." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163620"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Music History/Appreciation" ;
  skos:definition "Music History/Appreciation courses survey different musical styles and periods with the intent of increasing students' understanding of music and its importance in relation to the human experience. Music History/Appreciation courses may focus on how various styles of music apply musical elements to create an expressive or aesthetic impact. Students also have the ability for informal music performance and creation within the classroom." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05116" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Music History/Appreciation" .

ceds:NI001517163621
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Music History courses provide students with an understanding of music, its
			importance, and context in a selected range of historical periods and/or cultural
			styles. Students also have the ability for informal music performance and creation
			within the classroom.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163621"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Music History" ;
  skos:definition """Music History courses provide students with an understanding of music, its
