ceds:NI001517163923
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Audio/Visual Production courses provide students with the knowledge and
			skills necessary for television, video, film, and/or radio production. Writing scripts,
			camera operation, use of graphics and other visuals, lighting, audio techniques,
			editing, production principles, and career opportunities are typical topics covered
			within production courses. Students are usually required to produce their own program or
			segment. Additional topics such as broadcast industry regulations, radio/TV operation,
			power of the medium, photography, transmission technology, and so on may be included.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163923"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Audio/Visual Production" ;
  skos:definition """Audio/Visual Production courses provide students with the knowledge and
			skills necessary for television, video, film, and/or radio production. Writing scripts,
			camera operation, use of graphics and other visuals, lighting, audio techniques,
			editing, production principles, and career opportunities are typical topics covered
			within production courses. Students are usually required to produce their own program or
			segment. Additional topics such as broadcast industry regulations, radio/TV operation,
			power of the medium, photography, transmission technology, and so on may be included.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11051" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Audio/Visual Production" .

ceds:NI001517163924
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Commercial Photography courses provide instruction in the use of cameras and
			laboratory film- processing techniques. Topics covered in the course include composition
			and color dynamics; contact printing; enlarging; developing audio and visual images; use
			of camera meters, air brushes, and other photographic equipment; portrait, commercial,
			and industrial photography; processing microfilm; and preparing copy for printing or for
			graphic arts processing.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163924"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Commercial Photography" ;
  skos:definition """Commercial Photography courses provide instruction in the use of cameras
			and laboratory film- processing techniques. Topics covered in the course include
			composition and color dynamics; contact printing; enlarging; developing audio and visual
			images; use of camera meters, air brushes, and other photographic equipment; portrait,
			commercial, and industrial photography; processing microfilm; and preparing copy for
			printing or for graphic arts processing.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11052" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Commercial Photography" .

ceds:NI001517163925
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Photographic Laboratory and Darkroom courses prepare students to develop and
			print still or motion picture film. Topics covered in the course may include controlling
			resultant prints; touching up negatives; and finishing, coloring, restoring, and copying
			prints.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163925"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Photographic Laboratory and Darkroom" ;
  skos:definition """Photographic Laboratory and Darkroom courses prepare students to develop
			and print still or motion picture film. Topics covered in the course may include
			controlling resultant prints; touching up negatives; and finishing, coloring, restoring,
			and copying prints.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11053" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Photographic Laboratory and Darkroom" .

ceds:NI001517163926
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Photo Imaging courses provide students with the opportunity to effectively
			communicate ideas and information via digital, film, still and video photography. Topics
			covered typically include composition, layout, lighting and supplies. More advanced
			courses may include instruction in specialized camera and equipment maintenance,
			application to commercial and industrial need and photography business operations.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163926"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Photo Imaging" ;
  skos:definition """Photo Imaging courses provide students with the opportunity to effectively
			communicate ideas and information via digital, film, still and video photography. Topics
			covered typically include composition, layout, lighting and supplies. More advanced
			courses may include instruction in specialized camera and equipment maintenance,
			application to commercial and industrial need and photography business operations.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11054" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Photo Imaging" .

ceds:NI001517163927
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Video courses enable students to explore video communications, incorporating
			both the technical and artistic aspects of video media. Topics covered in the course
			include the use of video equipment and techniques, and students typically create a video
			presentation. Advanced course topics may include creating various forms of film media
			including silent film; sport and music video; and self portrait video.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163927"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Video" ;
  skos:definition """Video courses enable students to explore video communications,
			incorporating both the technical and artistic aspects of video media. Topics covered in
			the course include the use of video equipment and techniques, and students typically
			create a video presentation. Advanced course topics may include creating various forms
			of film media including silent film; sport and music video; and self portrait video.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11055" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Video" .

ceds:NI001517163928
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Broadcasting Technology courses provide students with the knowledge and
			skills to produce television broadcast programs. Typically, students prepare and produce
			short programs, learning the technical aspects of the operation and how to evaluate
			programming and assess audience reaction and impact.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163928"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Broadcasting Technology" ;
  skos:definition """Broadcasting Technology courses provide students with the knowledge and
			skills to produce television broadcast programs. Typically, students prepare and produce
			short programs, learning the technical aspects of the operation and how to evaluate
			programming and assess audience reaction and impact.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11103" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Broadcasting Technology" .

ceds:NI001517163929
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Publication Production courses provide students with the knowledge and
			skills necessary to produce the school newspaper, yearbook, literary magazine, or other
			printed publication. Students may gain experience in several components (writing,
			editing, layout, production, and so on) or may focus on a single aspect while producing
			the publication.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163929"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Publication Production" ;
  skos:definition """Publication Production courses provide students with the knowledge and
			skills necessary to produce the school newspaper, yearbook, literary magazine, or other
			printed publication. Students may gain experience in several components (writing,
			editing, layout, production, and so on) or may focus on a single aspect while producing
			the publication.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11104" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Publication Production" .

ceds:NI001517163930
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses examine specific topics in journalism and broadcasting other
			than those already described elsewhere in this classification system.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163930"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Journalism and Broadcasting" ;
  skos:definition """These courses examine specific topics in journalism and broadcasting other
			than those already described elsewhere in this classification system.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11105" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Journalism and Broadcasting" .

ceds:NI001517163931
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Emerging Technologies in Journalism courses promote the development of the
			necessary skills for journalism. Course topics may include an exploration of the role
			media and the communications industry has in society, technical skills related to
			journalistic writing and interviewing, electronic communications, journalistic blogging,
			and the ethical and legal issues related to technology in media and communications.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163931"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Emerging Technologies in Journalism" ;
  skos:definition """Emerging Technologies in Journalism courses promote the development of the
			necessary skills for journalism. Course topics may include an exploration of the role
			media and the communications industry has in society, technical skills related to
			journalistic writing and interviewing, electronic communications, journalistic blogging,
			and the ethical and legal issues related to technology in media and communications.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11106" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Emerging Technologies in Journalism" .

ceds:NI001517163932
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Radio Production courses address practices related to the management and
			operation of a broadcasting station. Students are introduced to the radio industry, news
			reporting, and broadcast engineering. In these courses, students learn basic electricity
			and electronics, including all aspects of safety. Topics typically include operating
			audio boards, announcing, creating and producing audio scripts, and using digital audio
			software. Advanced courses may explore direct programming, on-air performance, and
			analysis of ratio markets.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163932"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Radio Production" ;
  skos:definition """Radio Production courses address practices related to the management and
			operation of a broadcasting station. Students are introduced to the radio industry, news
			reporting, and broadcast engineering. In these courses, students learn basic electricity
			and electronics, including all aspects of safety. Topics typically include operating
			audio boards, announcing, creating and producing audio scripts, and using digital audio
			software. Advanced courses may explore direct programming, on-air performance, and
			analysis of ratio markets.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11107" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Radio Production" .

ceds:NI001517163933
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Journalism and Broadcasting—Independent Study courses, often conducted with
			instructors as mentors, enable students to explore topics of interest related to
			journalism, broadcasting, and mass media. Independent Study courses may serve as an
			opportunity for students to expand their expertise in a particular application, to
			explore a topic in greater detail, or to develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163933"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Journalism and Broadcasting—Independent Study" ;
  skos:definition """Journalism and Broadcasting—Independent Study courses, often conducted with
			instructors as mentors, enable students to explore topics of interest related to
			journalism, broadcasting, and mass media. Independent Study courses may serve as an
			opportunity for students to expand their expertise in a particular application, to
			explore a topic in greater detail, or to develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11147" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Journalism and Broadcasting—Independent Study" .

ceds:NI001517163934
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Journalism and Broadcasting—Workplace Experience courses provide students
			with work experience in a field related to journalism or broadcasting. Goals are
			typically set cooperatively by the student, teacher, and employer (although students are
			not necessarily paid). These courses may include classroom activities as well, involving
			further study of the field or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter
			in the workplace.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163934"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Journalism and Broadcasting—Workplace Experience" ;
  skos:definition """Journalism and Broadcasting—Workplace Experience courses provide students
			with work experience in a field related to journalism or broadcasting. Goals are
			typically set cooperatively by the student, teacher, and employer (although students are
			not necessarily paid). These courses may include classroom activities as well, involving
			further study of the field or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter
			in the workplace.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11148" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Journalism and Broadcasting—Workplace Experience" .

ceds:NI001517163935
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Other Journalism and Broadcasting courses." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163935"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Journalism and Broadcasting—Other" ;
  skos:definition "Other Journalism and Broadcasting courses." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11149" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Journalism and Broadcasting—Other" .

ceds:NI001517163936
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses are designed to give students the skills necessary to support
			and enhance their learning about digital medial technology. Topics covered in the course
			may include internet research, copyright laws, web-publishing, use of digital imagery,
			electronic forums, newsgroups, mailing lists, presentation tools, and project planning.""" ;
