ceds:NI001517163943
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Word Processing courses introduce students to automated document production
			using one or more software packages. These courses may introduce keyboarding techniques
			or may require prior experience. A parallel focus is placed on the use of software
			commands and functions to create, edit, format, and manipulate documents, capitalizing
			on the power offered by word processing software programs. These courses may also cover
			file and disk management and other computer-related skills.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163943"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Word Processing" ;
  skos:definition """Word Processing courses introduce students to automated document production
			using one or more software packages. These courses may introduce keyboarding techniques
			or may require prior experience. A parallel focus is placed on the use of software
			commands and functions to create, edit, format, and manipulate documents, capitalizing
			on the power offered by word processing software programs. These courses may also cover
			file and disk management and other computer-related skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "12006" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Word Processing" .

ceds:NI001517163944
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Recordkeeping courses help students develop knowledge and skills related to
			the principles and procedures involved in recording personal financial transactions as
			well as transactions typically undertaken by small businesses. Emphasis may be placed on
			software packages for accounting, database management, personal banking, budgeting, and
			income tax calculations. Additional emphasis is usually placed on cashier and clerk
			procedures, inventory control for small businesses, database management, merchandising,
			and payroll.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163944"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Recordkeeping" ;
  skos:definition """Recordkeeping courses help students develop knowledge and skills related to
			the principles and procedures involved in recording personal financial transactions as
			well as transactions typically undertaken by small businesses. Emphasis may be placed on
			software packages for accounting, database management, personal banking, budgeting, and
			income tax calculations. Additional emphasis is usually placed on cashier and clerk
			procedures, inventory control for small businesses, database management, merchandising,
			and payroll.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "12007" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Recordkeeping" .

ceds:NI001517163945
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Communication and Audio/Video Technology—Workplace Experience courses
			provide students with work experience in a field related to communication or
			audio/visual technology. Goals are typically set cooperatively by the student, teacher,
			and employer (although students are not necessarily paid). These courses may include
