ceds:NI001517164281
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Agriculture Mechanics/Equipment/Structures courses provide students with the
			skills and knowledge that are specifically applicable to the tools and equipment used in
			the industry. While learning to apply their knowledge of the basic principles of
			technological design and production skills (engine mechanics, power systems, welding,
			and carpentry, among others), students may explore a broad range of topics, including
			the operation, mechanics, and care of tools and machines; the construction and repair of
			structures integral to agricultural operations; a study of electricity and power
			principles; and the study of alternative fuels, technology and engineering, and safety
			procedures.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164281"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Agriculture Mechanics/Equipment/Structures" ;
  skos:definition """Agriculture Mechanics/Equipment/Structures courses provide students with
			the skills and knowledge that are specifically applicable to the tools and equipment
			used in the industry. While learning to apply their knowledge of the basic principles of
			technological design and production skills (engine mechanics, power systems, welding,
			and carpentry, among others), students may explore a broad range of topics, including
			the operation, mechanics, and care of tools and machines; the construction and repair of
			structures integral to agricultural operations; a study of electricity and power
			principles; and the study of alternative fuels, technology and engineering, and safety
			procedures.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "18401" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Agriculture Mechanics/Equipment/Structures" .

ceds:NI001517164282
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Agriculture Mechanics and Equipment courses provide students with the
			engineering, power, and mechanical technology principles, skills, and knowledge that are
			specifically applicable to the agricultural industry. Typical topics include the
			operation, maintenance, and repair of power, electrical, hydraulic, pneumatic,
			renewable, wind, solar, and mechanical systems.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164282"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Agriculture Mechanics and Equipment" ;
  skos:definition """Agriculture Mechanics and Equipment courses provide students with the
			engineering, power, and mechanical technology principles, skills, and knowledge that are
			specifically applicable to the agricultural industry. Typical topics include the
			operation, maintenance, and repair of power, electrical, hydraulic, pneumatic,
			renewable, wind, solar, and mechanical systems.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "18402" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Agriculture Mechanics and Equipment" .

ceds:NI001517164283
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Agriculture Structures courses provide students with the skills and
			knowledge that are specifically applicable to the construction, maintenance, and repair
			of structures integral to the agricultural industry, including but not limited to animal
			enclosures, irrigation systems, and storage facilities. In these courses, students
			typically study technology, design, planning, and construction knowledge and skills
			(such as measurement, carpentry, plumbing, concrete, and electrical systems), in
			addition to the safe operation of tools, technology and machines.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164283"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Agriculture Structures" ;
  skos:definition """Agriculture Structures courses provide students with the skills and
			knowledge that are specifically applicable to the construction, maintenance, and repair
			of structures integral to the agricultural industry, including but not limited to animal
			enclosures, irrigation systems, and storage facilities. In these courses, students
			typically study technology, design, planning, and construction knowledge and skills
			(such as measurement, carpentry, plumbing, concrete, and electrical systems), in
			addition to the safe operation of tools, technology and machines.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "18403" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Agriculture Structures" .

ceds:NI001517164284
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Formerly known as Agriculture Welding, Agricultural Metal Fabrication
			Technology courses provide students with the skills and knowledge that are specifically
			applicable to the tools and equipment used in the industry. In learning to apply basic
			technical knowledge and skills (engines, power, welding, and structures, among others),
			students may explore a broad range of topics, including the operation, mechanics, and
			care of tools, technology and machines; the construction and repair of structures
			integral to agricultural operations; an introduction or review of electricity and power;
			and safety procedures.""" ;
