			astronomic instruments and typically explore theories regarding the origin and evolution
			of the universe, space, and time.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "03004" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Astronomy" .

ceds:NI001517163326
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Courses in Marine Science focus on the content, features, and possibilities of the earth's oceans. They explore marine organisms, conditions, and ecology and sometimes cover marine mining, farming, and exploration." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163326"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Marine Science" ;
  skos:definition "Courses in Marine Science focus on the content, features, and possibilities of the earth's oceans. They explore marine organisms, conditions, and ecology and sometimes cover marine mining, farming, and exploration." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "03005" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Marine Science" .

ceds:NI001517163327
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Meteorology courses examine the properties of the earth's atmosphere. Topics usually include atmospheric layering, changing pressures, winds, water vapor, air masses, fronts, temperature changes and weather forecasting." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163327"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Meteorology" ;
  skos:definition "Meteorology courses examine the properties of the earth's atmosphere. Topics usually include atmospheric layering, changing pressures, winds, water vapor, air masses, fronts, temperature changes and weather forecasting." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "03006" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Meteorology" .

ceds:NI001517163328
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Physical Geography courses equip students with an understanding of the
			constraints and possibilities that the physical environment places on human development.
			These courses include discussion of the physical landscape through geomorphology and
			topography, the patterns and processes of climate and weather, and natural resources.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163328"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Physical Geography" ;
  skos:definition """Physical Geography courses equip students with an understanding of the
