			explore a topic in greater detail, or to develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "19247" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Apparel and Furnishings—Independent Study" .

ceds:NI001517164338
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Apparel and Furnishings—Workplace Experience courses provide students with
			work experience in fields related to apparel, textiles, and furnishings. Goals are
			typically set cooperatively by the student, teacher, and employer (although students are
			not necessarily paid). These courses may include classroom activities as well, involving
			further study of the field or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter
			in the workplace.""" ;
