ceds:NI001517163351
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB Sports, Exercise, and Health Science courses prepare students to take the
			International Baccalaureate Sports, Exercise, and Health Science exam. These courses are
			designed to provide students with an understanding of the science of physical
			performance. Course topics may include anatomy and physiology, biomechanics, psychology
			and nutrition, and the measurement and evaluation of human performance.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163351"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Sports, Exercise, and Health Science" ;
  skos:definition """IB Sports, Exercise, and Health Science courses prepare students to take
			the International Baccalaureate Sports, Exercise, and Health Science exam. These courses
			are designed to provide students with an understanding of the science of physical
			performance. Course topics may include anatomy and physiology, biomechanics, psychology
			and nutrition, and the measurement and evaluation of human performance.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "03065" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Sports, Exercise, and Health Science" .

ceds:NI001517163352
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum, PLTW Principles of Biomedical Science courses focus on a case study in which students investigate the cause of death of a fictional person. Students conduct research, in which they examine autopsy reports, review medical history, and study human physiology, biology, and medicine to diagnose and recommend treatments that could have been applied." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163352"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "PLTW Principles of Biomedical Science" ;
  skos:definition "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum, PLTW Principles of Biomedical Science courses focus on a case study in which students investigate the cause of death of a fictional person. Students conduct research, in which they examine autopsy reports, review medical history, and study human physiology, biology, and medicine to diagnose and recommend treatments that could have been applied." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "03066" ;
  skos:prefLabel "PLTW Principles of Biomedical Science" .

