ceds:NI001517163694
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Formerly known as Integrated Fine Arts, Interdisciplinary Arts courses
			explore communication across the arts disciplines: any subset or all of the visual arts,
			music, drama, theater, dance, and literature may be addressed in the curriculum for
			these courses. Students study and critique the works of others and participate in or
			produce art themselves. These courses often include comparative study of various art
			forms over time (i.e., the interrelationship of theater and visual arts of a particular
			time period and culture).""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163694"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Interdisciplinary Arts" ;
  skos:definition """Formerly known as Integrated Fine Arts, Interdisciplinary Arts courses
			explore communication across the arts disciplines: any subset or all of the visual arts,
			music, drama, theater, dance, and literature may be addressed in the curriculum for
			these courses. Students study and critique the works of others and participate in or
			produce art themselves. These courses often include comparative study of various art
			forms over time (i.e., the interrelationship of theater and visual arts of a particular
			time period and culture).""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05201" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Interdisciplinary Arts" .

ceds:NI001517163695
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """International Baccalaureate (IB) Arts, Middle Years Program courses include
			visual and performing arts and organize learning around the creative cycle. These
			courses bring students into contact with art forms and aesthetic values of several
			cultures and help students master artistic techniques.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163695"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Arts, Middle Years Program" ;
  skos:definition """International Baccalaureate (IB) Arts, Middle Years Program courses include
			visual and performing arts and organize learning around the creative cycle. These
			courses bring students into contact with art forms and aesthetic values of several
			cultures and help students master artistic techniques.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05202" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Arts, Middle Years Program" .

ceds:NI001517163696
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Film Appreciation and Analysis courses help students understand the critical
			historical and stylistic elements of cinema. These courses help students form an
			aesthetic framework to examine social, political, and historical events in the world and
			to understand how moving images express the ideas of individuals and society. Course
			content may include analysis, discussion, and evaluation of multiple film styles
			including, but not limited to, documentary, short film, drama, horror, and comedy.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163696"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Film Appreciation and Analysis" ;
  skos:definition """Film Appreciation and Analysis courses help students understand the
			critical historical and stylistic elements of cinema. These courses help students form
			an aesthetic framework to examine social, political, and historical events in the world
			and to understand how moving images express the ideas of individuals and society. Course
			content may include analysis, discussion, and evaluation of multiple film styles
			including, but not limited to, documentary, short film, drama, horror, and comedy.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05203" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Film Appreciation and Analysis" .

