ceds:NI001517163712
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Religious Foundations courses' primary objectives include instruction in the history, tenets, and organization of a religion; development of personal faith and conviction; and exposure to the ways in which daily life may reflect personal religious beliefs. These courses typically include various components particular to a specific religion, such as religious sacraments and symbols, food laws, the authority and structure of the church, the church calendar, and so on." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163712"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Religious Foundations" ;
  skos:definition "Religious Foundations courses' primary objectives include instruction in the history, tenets, and organization of a religion; development of personal faith and conviction; and exposure to the ways in which daily life may reflect personal religious beliefs. These courses typically include various components particular to a specific religion, such as religious sacraments and symbols, food laws, the authority and structure of the church, the church calendar, and so on." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "07001" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Religious Foundations" .

ceds:NI001517163713
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Comparative Religion courses survey and compare the various forms and values of several world religions, offering students a basic understanding of the world's diverse religious faiths and practices. Course topics typically include the belief systems of adherents; the relationships among humans, nature, ancestors, and the spiritual world; and the historical development of each religion." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163713"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Comparative Religion" ;
  skos:definition "Comparative Religion courses survey and compare the various forms and values of several world religions, offering students a basic understanding of the world's diverse religious faiths and practices. Course topics typically include the belief systems of adherents; the relationships among humans, nature, ancestors, and the spiritual world; and the historical development of each religion." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "07002" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Comparative Religion" .

ceds:NI001517163714
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Similar to Comparative Religion, Eastern Religions courses provide students
			with an overview of various religions and belief systems but focus on those of the
			Eastern World. Particular religious or philosophical systems of study usually include
			Buddhism, Hinduism, Islam, Taoism, Shintoism, and Confucianism, among others.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163714"^^xsd:token ;
