ceds:NI001517164023
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Production Systems courses provide students with knowledge and skills related to manufacturing technologies from conception through production. Although courses vary, students typically analyze markets, design and develop prototypes, plan a marketing or sales strategy, manage a production plan, and manufacture useful products. These courses may also explore the evolution and impact of technology on society's social, cultural, and economic systems and institutions." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164023"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Production Systems" ;
  skos:definition "Production Systems courses provide students with knowledge and skills related to manufacturing technologies from conception through production. Although courses vary, students typically analyze markets, design and develop prototypes, plan a marketing or sales strategy, manage a production plan, and manufacture useful products. These courses may also explore the evolution and impact of technology on society's social, cultural, and economic systems and institutions." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13101" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Production Systems" .

ceds:NI001517164024
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Electro-Mechanical Systems courses provide students with instruction and
			experience in components and equipment used within a manufacturing environment powered
			by electricity and physical forces. Students gain an understanding of basic and
			industrial electricity, industrial electronics, and the automated systems used in the
			manufacturing process or within manufactured goods.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164024"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Electro-Mechanical Systems" ;
  skos:definition """Electro-Mechanical Systems courses provide students with instruction and
			experience in components and equipment used within a manufacturing environment powered
			by electricity and physical forces. Students gain an understanding of basic and
			industrial electricity, industrial electronics, and the automated systems used in the
			manufacturing process or within manufactured goods.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13102" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Electro-Mechanical Systems" .

ceds:NI001517164025
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Product Development courses provide students with the opportunity to focus
			on one or more areas of industrial technology to design or redesign a product to solve a
			problem. Students may build prototypes and working models and may evaluate the product
			and process according to industry standards.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164025"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Product Development" ;
  skos:definition """Product Development courses provide students with the opportunity to focus
			on one or more areas of industrial technology to design or redesign a product to solve a
			problem. Students may build prototypes and working models and may evaluate the product
			and process according to industry standards.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13103" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Product Development" .

ceds:NI001517164026
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Metal Processing/Production courses allow students to study the physical and
			chemical properties of metals and metal alloys and to use these materials to construct
			usable products according to industry standards. These courses enable students to
			experience the process of translating an idea into a finished product, with instruction
			in planning, designing, selecting materials, and using tools and machines.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164026"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Metal Processing/Production" ;
  skos:definition """Metal Processing/Production courses allow students to study the physical
			and chemical properties of metals and metal alloys and to use these materials to
			construct usable products according to industry standards. These courses enable students
			to experience the process of translating an idea into a finished product, with
			instruction in planning, designing, selecting materials, and using tools and machines.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13055" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Metal Processing/Production" .

