			are not necessarily paid). These courses may include classroom activities as well,
			involving further study of the field or discussion regarding experiences that students
			encounter in the workplace.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13348" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Repair—Workplace Experience" .

ceds:NI001517164035
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Sheet Metal courses expose students to the skills and information necessary
			to lay out, fabricate, assemble, install, maintain, and repair items and structures
			created from sheet metal components. Students learn the safe and efficient operation of
			various tools and typically gain skill in blueprint reading, welding, and finishing and
			polishing metals.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164035"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Sheet Metal" ;
  skos:definition """Sheet Metal courses expose students to the skills and information necessary
			to lay out, fabricate, assemble, install, maintain, and repair items and structures
			created from sheet metal components. Students learn the safe and efficient operation of
			various tools and typically gain skill in blueprint reading, welding, and finishing and
			polishing metals.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13205" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Sheet Metal" .

ceds:NI001517164036
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """In these courses students gain knowledge and skills in particular aspects of
			sheet metal. Examples include individual courses in radial line development,
			triangulation fabrication, and so on.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164036"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Sheet Metal" ;
  skos:definition """In these courses students gain knowledge and skills in particular aspects
			of sheet metal. Examples include individual courses in radial line development,
			triangulation fabrication, and so on.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13206" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Sheet Metal" .

ceds:NI001517164037
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Welding courses enable students to gain knowledge of the physical and
			chemical properties, uses, and applications of various metals. Students gain skills in
			various processes used to join and cut metals (such as oxyacetylene, shielded metal,
			metal inert gas, and tungsten arc processes) and experience in identifying, selecting,
			and rating appropriate techniques. Students read and interpret blueprints in order to
			identify, select, and rate appropriate techniques. These courses may prepare students to
			pass relevant industry certifications.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164037"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Welding" ;
  skos:definition """Welding courses enable students to gain knowledge of the physical and
			chemical properties, uses, and applications of various metals. Students gain skills in
			various processes used to join and cut metals (such as oxyacetylene, shielded metal,
			metal inert gas, and tungsten arc processes) and experience in identifying, selecting,
			and rating appropriate techniques. Students read and interpret blueprints in order to
			identify, select, and rate appropriate techniques. These courses may prepare students to
			pass relevant industry certifications.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13207" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Welding" .

ceds:NI001517164038
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """In these courses students gain knowledge and skills in particular aspects of
			welding. Examples include individual courses in each of the following types of welding:
			gas metal, gas tungsten, and shielded metal and flux core arc welding.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164038"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Welding" ;
  skos:definition """In these courses students gain knowledge and skills in particular aspects
			of welding. Examples include individual courses in each of the following types of
			welding: gas metal, gas tungsten, and shielded metal and flux core arc welding.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13208" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Welding" .

