ceds:NI001517164371
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Automotive Body Repair and Refinishing courses provide students with
			knowledge and skills regarding the repair and refinishing of damaged or used cars.
			Course content may include (but is not limited to) stretching and shrinking auto body
			sheet metal; welding skills; frame and metal straightening; repair of fiberglass and
			synthetic materials; removing, repairing, and installing auto body parts such as panels,
			hoods, doors, and windows/glass; preparing vehicles and vehicle surfaces for
			refinishing; painting; applying body fillers; and estimating material and labor costs.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164371"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Automotive Body Repair and Refinishing—Comprehensive" ;
  skos:definition """Automotive Body Repair and Refinishing courses provide students with
			knowledge and skills regarding the repair and refinishing of damaged or used cars.
			Course content may include (but is not limited to) stretching and shrinking auto body
			sheet metal; welding skills; frame and metal straightening; repair of fiberglass and
			synthetic materials; removing, repairing, and installing auto body parts such as panels,
			hoods, doors, and windows/glass; preparing vehicles and vehicle surfaces for
			refinishing; painting; applying body fillers; and estimating material and labor costs.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20116" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Automotive Body Repair and Refinishing—Comprehensive" .

ceds:NI001517164372
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses provide specific instruction in individual topics relevant to
			the repair and refinishing of automobile bodies and surfaces. One topic or several
			closely related topics (such as nonstructural part replacement, auto body welding, or
			plastic repair) receive particular attention in this type of course.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164372"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Automotive Body Repair and Refinishing" ;
  skos:definition """These courses provide specific instruction in individual topics relevant to
			the repair and refinishing of automobile bodies and surfaces. One topic or several
			closely related topics (such as nonstructural part replacement, auto body welding, or
			plastic repair) receive particular attention in this type of course.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20117" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Automotive Body Repair and Refinishing" .

ceds:NI001517164373
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Boat Repair/Refinishing courses convey a broad range of information and
			skills about how to repair and refinish boat mechanics, structures, and surfaces. In
			these courses, students become proficient in marine terminology, learn how to describe
			types of marine manufacturing and occupations, and prepare new and existing wood,
			fiberglass, and metal surfaces for painting or refinishing. These courses often cover
			safety, employability skills, and entrepreneurship.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164373"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Boat Repair/Refinishing" ;
  skos:definition """Boat Repair/Refinishing courses convey a broad range of information and
			skills about how to repair and refinish boat mechanics, structures, and surfaces. In
			these courses, students become proficient in marine terminology, learn how to describe
			types of marine manufacturing and occupations, and prepare new and existing wood,
			fiberglass, and metal surfaces for painting or refinishing. These courses often cover
			safety, employability skills, and entrepreneurship.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20118" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Boat Repair/Refinishing" .

ceds:NI001517164374
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Exploration of Transportation, Distribution, and Logistics courses introduce
			students to careers that involve the planning, management, and movement of people,
			materials, and products using any of several modes of transport. Such careers may also
			involve infrastructure, vehicular maintenance and repair, and operating or managing
			facilities that hold what is being transported. Therefore, specific course topics vary
			widely and depend upon the careers being explored.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164374"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Exploration of Transportation, Distribution and Logistics" ;
  skos:definition """Exploration of Transportation, Distribution, and Logistics courses
			introduce students to careers that involve the planning, management, and movement of
			people, materials, and products using any of several modes of transport. Such careers
			may also involve infrastructure, vehicular maintenance and repair, and operating or
			managing facilities that hold what is being transported. Therefore, specific course
			topics vary widely and depend upon the careers being explored.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20001" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Exploration of Transportation, Distribution and Logistics" .

ceds:NI001517164375
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Truck and Bus Driving courses instruct students in the proper and safe
			handling and operation of trucks and buses. Strategies for driving in hazardous
			conditions, observing laws and regulations, loading cargo or passengers, documenting
			cargo loads, and expectations of driving careers are all typical course topics.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164375"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Truck and Bus Driving" ;
  skos:definition """Truck and Bus Driving courses instruct students in the proper and safe
			handling and operation of trucks and buses. Strategies for driving in hazardous
			conditions, observing laws and regulations, loading cargo or passengers, documenting
			cargo loads, and expectations of driving careers are all typical course topics.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20051" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Truck and Bus Driving" .

ceds:NI001517164376
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Heavy Equipment Operation courses enable students to safely operate the
			heavy equipment used for mining, construction, and utility industries. Typically,
			courses also include light maintenance principles and techniques.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164376"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Heavy Equipment Operation" ;
  skos:definition """Heavy Equipment Operation courses enable students to safely operate the
			heavy equipment used for mining, construction, and utility industries. Typically,
			courses also include light maintenance principles and techniques.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20052" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Heavy Equipment Operation" .

ceds:NI001517164377
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Aviation courses provide students with an understanding of the science of
			flight and typically include the history, regulations, and possible career paths within
			the aviation industry. Aviation courses usually cover physics, the relationships of
			weight and balance, principles of navigation and flight control, ground and airport
			operations and services, and Federal Aviation Agency regulations.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164377"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Aviation" ;
  skos:definition """Aviation courses provide students with an understanding of the science of
			flight and typically include the history, regulations, and possible career paths within
			the aviation industry. Aviation courses usually cover physics, the relationships of
			weight and balance, principles of navigation and flight control, ground and airport
			operations and services, and Federal Aviation Agency regulations.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20053" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Aviation" .

ceds:NI001517164378
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Boat Operation courses typically cover operation and maintenance of marine
			vehicles, marine navigation, and emergency procedures, as well as other skills necessary
			or useful for work or life at sea (e.g., loading and unloading or cooking). Specific
			topics may include docking and undocking a vessel, engine maintenance, commercial
			fishing, firefighting aboard ship, and CPR.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164378"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Boat Operation" ;
  skos:definition """Boat Operation courses typically cover operation and maintenance of marine
			vehicles, marine navigation, and emergency procedures, as well as other skills necessary
			or useful for work or life at sea (e.g., loading and unloading or cooking). Specific
			topics may include docking and undocking a vessel, engine maintenance, commercial
			fishing, firefighting aboard ship, and CPR.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20054" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Boat Operation" .

ceds:NI001517164379
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Pilot Training courses prepare students to become pilots by participating in
			flight training, ground school, and simulator instruction. Topics covered typically
			include preflight operations; flight maneuvering with reference to ground objects;
			flying at critically slow air speeds and recovering from stalls; takeoffs and landings;
			controlling and maneuvering an aircraft; cross country flying; night flying; and
			emergency operation. Other course content may include meteorology, aerodynamics,
			navigation, physiology, and airfield and flight environments.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164379"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Pilot Training" ;
  skos:definition """Pilot Training courses prepare students to become pilots by participating
			in flight training, ground school, and simulator instruction. Topics covered typically
			include preflight operations; flight maneuvering with reference to ground objects;
			flying at critically slow air speeds and recovering from stalls; takeoffs and landings;
			controlling and maneuvering an aircraft; cross country flying; night flying; and
			emergency operation. Other course content may include meteorology, aerodynamics,
			navigation, physiology, and airfield and flight environments.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20055" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Pilot Training" .

ceds:NI001517164380
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Operation—Independent Study courses, often conducted with instructors as
			mentors, enable students to explore topics of interest related to the operation of
			vehicles. Independent Study courses may serve as an opportunity for students to expand
			their expertise in a particular application, to explore a topic in greater detail, or to
			develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164380"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Operation—Independent Study" ;
  skos:definition """Operation—Independent Study courses, often conducted with instructors as
			mentors, enable students to explore topics of interest related to the operation of
			vehicles. Independent Study courses may serve as an opportunity for students to expand
			their expertise in a particular application, to explore a topic in greater detail, or to
			develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20097" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Operation—Independent Study" .

ceds:NI001517164381
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Operation—Workplace Experience courses provide students with work experience
			in fields related to the operation of vehicles. Goals are typically set cooperatively by
			the student, teacher, and employer (although students are not necessarily paid). These
			courses may include classroom activities as well, involving further study of the field
			or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter in the workplace.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164381"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Operation—Workplace Experience" ;
  skos:definition """Operation—Workplace Experience courses provide students with work
			experience in fields related to the operation of vehicles. Goals are typically set
			cooperatively by the student, teacher, and employer (although students are not
			necessarily paid). These courses may include classroom activities as well, involving
			further study of the field or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter
			in the workplace.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20098" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Operation—Workplace Experience" .

