ceds:NI001517163724
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Usually including an introduction to or examination of the tenets of a
			particular faith, Religious Ethics and Morality courses seek to enable students to apply
			the moral teachings of a faith to their own lives, to the larger community, and to their
			decision-making processes. Course content may focus on such issues as peace and justice,
			death and dying, human sexuality, professional ethics, and human rights.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163724"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Religious Ethics and Morality" ;
  skos:definition """Usually including an introduction to or examination of the tenets of a
			particular faith, Religious Ethics and Morality courses seek to enable students to apply
			the moral teachings of a faith to their own lives, to the larger community, and to their
			decision-making processes. Course content may focus on such issues as peace and justice,
			death and dying, human sexuality, professional ethics, and human rights.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "07013" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Religious Ethics and Morality" .

ceds:NI001517163725
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Justice, Peace, and Faith courses examine the scriptural foundations for justice, typically with a historical overview of a faith's social teaching. These courses discuss such topics as poverty, hunger, conflict, discrimination, justice, and environmental issues, with a view toward developing students' ability to critically reflect upon and analyze their own roles and responsibilities." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163725"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Justice, Peace, and Faith" ;
  skos:definition "Justice, Peace, and Faith courses examine the scriptural foundations for justice, typically with a historical overview of a faith's social teaching. These courses discuss such topics as poverty, hunger, conflict, discrimination, justice, and environmental issues, with a view toward developing students' ability to critically reflect upon and analyze their own roles and responsibilities." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "07014" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Justice, Peace, and Faith" .

ceds:NI001517163726
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Faith and Lifestyle courses focus on the development of young adults from puberty to adulthood, approached from the perspective of a faith or church. In these courses, the religion's values and traditions provide an underpinning for examining such topics as identity, independence, sexuality, employment, and leisure. Typically, Faith and Lifestyle courses include discussions about adult roles— single life, marriage, religious life, and ordained ministry." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163726"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Faith and Lifestyle" ;
  skos:definition "Faith and Lifestyle courses focus on the development of young adults from puberty to adulthood, approached from the perspective of a faith or church. In these courses, the religion's values and traditions provide an underpinning for examining such topics as identity, independence, sexuality, employment, and leisure. Typically, Faith and Lifestyle courses include discussions about adult roles— single life, marriage, religious life, and ordained ministry." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "07015" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Faith and Lifestyle" .

ceds:NI001517163727
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Ministry courses introduce students to the vocation of service. Students may
			learn counseling skills, plan and participate in religious services, and minister to
			younger students or to members of the local community (assisting in hospitals and
			convalescent homes, crisis centers, soup kitchens, and so on).""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163727"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Ministry" ;
  skos:definition """Ministry courses introduce students to the vocation of service. Students
