			convalescent homes, crisis centers, soup kitchens, and so on).""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "07016" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Ministry" .

ceds:NI001517163728
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB World Religions courses prepare students to take the International
			Baccalaureate exam. These courses are designed to provide students with the means to
			study the beliefs and practices of nine main religions of the world. These courses may
			include an in-depth study of several religions with an emphasis on thematic elements. An
			investigative study of the religious experience is also included.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163728"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB World Religions" ;
  skos:definition """IB World Religions courses prepare students to take the International
			Baccalaureate exam. These courses are designed to provide students with the means to
