ceds:NI001517163748
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Topics covered within Health Education courses may vary widely, but
			typically include personal health (nutrition, mental health and stress management,
			drug/alcohol abuse prevention, disease prevention, and first aid) and consumer health
			issues. The courses may also include brief studies of environmental health, personal
			development, and/or community resources.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163748"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Health Education" ;
  skos:definition """Topics covered within Health Education courses may vary widely, but
			typically include personal health (nutrition, mental health and stress management,
			drug/alcohol abuse prevention, disease prevention, and first aid) and consumer health
			issues. The courses may also include brief studies of environmental health, personal
			development, and/or community resources.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "08051" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Health Education" .

ceds:NI001517163749
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Health and Fitness courses combine the topics of Health Education courses
			(nutrition, stress management, substance abuse prevention, disease prevention, first
			aid, and so on) with an active fitness component (typically including aerobic activity
			and fitness circuits) with the intention of conveying the importance of life-long
			wellness habits.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163749"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Health and Fitness" ;
  skos:definition """Health and Fitness courses combine the topics of Health Education courses
			(nutrition, stress management, substance abuse prevention, disease prevention, first
			aid, and so on) with an active fitness component (typically including aerobic activity
			and fitness circuits) with the intention of conveying the importance of life-long
			wellness habits.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "08052" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Health and Fitness" .

ceds:NI001517163750
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Community Health courses cover not only personal health topics (nutrition, stress management, substance abuse prevention, disease prevention, first aid, and so on), but also more general health issues. These additional topics may include (among others) available community resources, fundamentals of the nation's health care system, contemporary world health issues, and career options within the health field." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163750"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Community Health" ;
  skos:definition "Community Health courses cover not only personal health topics (nutrition, stress management, substance abuse prevention, disease prevention, first aid, and so on), but also more general health issues. These additional topics may include (among others) available community resources, fundamentals of the nation's health care system, contemporary world health issues, and career options within the health field." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "08053" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Community Health" .

ceds:NI001517163751
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Physical Education (grade 8) courses typically involve the acquisition of
			knowledge and skills that provide the foundation for sport, a physically active
			lifestyle, and social development through physical activity. Activities typically
			include those that increase strength, endurance, and flexibility; reinforce safe
			technique; teach the rules and conventions of games and sports; and explore the
			relationship between physical activity and health. Health topics (such as the effects of
			drugs and alcohol, sexual education, and healthy lifestyles) may also be included.
			Specific content depends upon state standards for grade 8.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163751"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Physical Education (grade 8)" ;
  skos:definition """Physical Education (grade 8) courses typically involve the acquisition of
			knowledge and skills that provide the foundation for sport, a physically active
			lifestyle, and social development through physical activity. Activities typically
			include those that increase strength, endurance, and flexibility; reinforce safe
			technique; teach the rules and conventions of games and sports; and explore the
			relationship between physical activity and health. Health topics (such as the effects of
			drugs and alcohol, sexual education, and healthy lifestyles) may also be included.
			Specific content depends upon state standards for grade 8.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "08038" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Physical Education (grade 8)" .

ceds:NI001517163752
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Physical Education—General courses involve content that is not grade
			differentiated and may apply to a range of consecutive grades (e.g., "by third grade,
			students should know and be able to do…"). These courses include content that may be
			applicable to states or localities that do not employ grade-level content standards.
			[These courses provide broad content that is not organized as described elsewhere (i.e.,
			Physical Education, early childhood education through grade 8).]""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163752"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Physical Education—General" ;
  skos:definition """Physical Education—General courses involve content that is not grade
			differentiated and may apply to a range of consecutive grades (e.g., "by third grade,
			students should know and be able to do…"). These courses include content that may be
			applicable to states or localities that do not employ grade-level content standards.
			[These courses provide broad content that is not organized as described elsewhere (i.e.,
			Physical Education, early childhood education through grade 8).]""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "08039" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Physical Education—General" .

ceds:NI001517163753
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """International Baccalaureate (IB) Physical and Health Education, Middle Years
			Program courses aim to facilitate physical, intellectual, emotional, and social
			development, and to cultivate a healthy and active lifestyle. These courses include
			activities that are enjoyable and contribute to healthy living. They help students
			develop motor skills necessary to participate in a variety of physical activities, and
			to learn about the nature of physical fitness.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163753"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Physical and Health Education, Middle Years Program" ;
