			provide basic experience in maintenance tasks. The course may also cover career
			opportunities in the automotive and/or transportation fields.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20103" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Introduction to Automobiles" .

ceds:NI001517164386
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Automotive Mechanics—Comprehensive courses emphasize the diagnosis and
			repair of automobile engines and support systems such as brakes, cooling, drive trains,
			electrical/electronics components, emission, fuel, ignition, steering, suspension, and
			transmissions. Course topics often include the comprehension and use of repair manuals,
			safety, and employability skills (including shop management and entrepreneurship).""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164386"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Automotive Mechanics—Comprehensive" ;
  skos:definition """Automotive Mechanics—Comprehensive courses emphasize the diagnosis and
			repair of automobile engines and support systems such as brakes, cooling, drive trains,
			electrical/electronics components, emission, fuel, ignition, steering, suspension, and
			transmissions. Course topics often include the comprehension and use of repair manuals,
			safety, and employability skills (including shop management and entrepreneurship).""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20104" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Automotive Mechanics—Comprehensive" .

ceds:NI001517164387
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses provide instruction in the mechanics of a particular system or
			condition, such as transmissions, brakes, fuel, exhaust, or electrical systems, rather
			than providing a general study of diagnosis and repair of automobile mechanics.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164387"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Automotive Mechanics" ;
  skos:definition """These courses provide instruction in the mechanics of a particular system
			or condition, such as transmissions, brakes, fuel, exhaust, or electrical systems,
			rather than providing a general study of diagnosis and repair of automobile mechanics.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20105" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Automotive Mechanics" .

ceds:NI001517164388
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Automotive Service courses emphasize preventative auto maintenance and
			automobile troubleshooting. Course content typically includes tune-up, oil change, and
			lubrication skills; tire replacement, alignment, and balancing; and basic knowledge of
			brake, cooling, electrical, emission, fuel, ignition, steering, suspension, and
			transmission systems. These courses may also include public relations, sales techniques,
			and service station management.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164388"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Automotive Service" ;
  skos:definition """Automotive Service courses emphasize preventative auto maintenance and
			automobile troubleshooting. Course content typically includes tune-up, oil change, and
			lubrication skills; tire replacement, alignment, and balancing; and basic knowledge of
			brake, cooling, electrical, emission, fuel, ignition, steering, suspension, and
			transmission systems. These courses may also include public relations, sales techniques,
			and service station management.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20106" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Automotive Service" .

ceds:NI001517164389
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Diesel Mechanics—Comprehensive courses prepare students to maintain and
			repair diesel engines and related systems. Specific course topics may include principles
			underlying diesel engines, analyzing electrical circuits and systems, troubleshooting
			and repairing cooling systems, testing and repairing air conditioning charging systems,
			reading and interpreting service manuals, and identifying the principles and components
			of fuel injection systems. Courses may also cover safety, employability skills, and
			entrepreneurship.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164389"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Diesel Mechanics—Comprehensive" ;
  skos:definition """Diesel Mechanics—Comprehensive courses prepare students to maintain and
			repair diesel engines and related systems. Specific course topics may include principles
			underlying diesel engines, analyzing electrical circuits and systems, troubleshooting
			and repairing cooling systems, testing and repairing air conditioning charging systems,
			reading and interpreting service manuals, and identifying the principles and components
			of fuel injection systems. Courses may also cover safety, employability skills, and
			entrepreneurship.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20107" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Diesel Mechanics—Comprehensive" .

ceds:NI001517164390
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses cover specific topics relevant to occupations involving the
			maintenance and repair of vehicles with diesel engines, such as buses and trucks. One
			topic (or several closely related topics) concerning diesel mechanics is covered in
			specific detail in this type of course.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164390"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Diesel Mechanics" ;
  skos:definition """These courses cover specific topics relevant to occupations involving the
			maintenance and repair of vehicles with diesel engines, such as buses and trucks. One
			topic (or several closely related topics) concerning diesel mechanics is covered in
			specific detail in this type of course.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20108" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Diesel Mechanics" .

ceds:NI001517164391
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Small Vehicle Mechanics courses equip students with the knowledge and skill
			to repair and maintain engines in small vehicles (e.g., motorcycles, all-terrain
			vehicles, snowmobiles, and mopeds). Topics include (but are not limited to) maintaining
			frames and suspension, wheels and brakes, and drive trains; servicing fuel, exhaust, and
			electrical systems; performing tune-ups; and maintaining and repairing engines. Students
			may also learn safety on the job, employability skills, and entrepreneurship.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164391"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Small Vehicle Mechanics" ;
  skos:definition """Small Vehicle Mechanics courses equip students with the knowledge and skill
			to repair and maintain engines in small vehicles (e.g., motorcycles, all-terrain
			vehicles, snowmobiles, and mopeds). Topics include (but are not limited to) maintaining
			frames and suspension, wheels and brakes, and drive trains; servicing fuel, exhaust, and
			electrical systems; performing tune-ups; and maintaining and repairing engines. Students
			may also learn safety on the job, employability skills, and entrepreneurship.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20109" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Small Vehicle Mechanics" .

ceds:NI001517164392
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Small Engine Mechanics courses provide students with the opportunity to learn how to service and recondition small engines, typically emphasizing two- and four-cycle engines. These courses provide students with opportunities to troubleshoot and repair speed controls, lubrication, ignition, fuel, power transfer, cooling, exhaust, and starting systems; use hand, power, and overhaul tools; and read and interpret service manuals and parts' catalogs. Applications may include lawn mowers, tractors, tillers, power tools, and so on." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164392"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Small Engine Mechanics" ;
  skos:definition "Small Engine Mechanics courses provide students with the opportunity to learn how to service and recondition small engines, typically emphasizing two- and four-cycle engines. These courses provide students with opportunities to troubleshoot and repair speed controls, lubrication, ignition, fuel, power transfer, cooling, exhaust, and starting systems; use hand, power, and overhaul tools; and read and interpret service manuals and parts' catalogs. Applications may include lawn mowers, tractors, tillers, power tools, and so on." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20110" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Small Engine Mechanics" .

ceds:NI001517164393
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """The content of Marine Mechanics courses includes the service and repair of
			electrical, mechanical, power transfer, hydraulic, fuel, and cooling systems as applied
			to boat and/or ship engines; boat rigging; trailers; and marine-related merchandise.
			Courses may also cover communication, human relations, and employability skills, as well
			as safe, efficient work practices.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164393"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Marine Mechanics" ;
  skos:definition """The content of Marine Mechanics courses includes the service and repair of
			electrical, mechanical, power transfer, hydraulic, fuel, and cooling systems as applied
			to boat and/or ship engines; boat rigging; trailers; and marine-related merchandise.
			Courses may also cover communication, human relations, and employability skills, as well
			as safe, efficient work practices.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20111" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Marine Mechanics" .

ceds:NI001517164394
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Heavy Equipment Mechanics courses include the service and repair of
			electrical, mechanical, power transfer, hydraulic, fuel, and cooling systems of heavy
			equipment such as that used in mining, construction, and utility industries.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164394"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Heavy Equipment Mechanics" ;
  skos:definition """Heavy Equipment Mechanics courses include the service and repair of
			electrical, mechanical, power transfer, hydraulic, fuel, and cooling systems of heavy
			equipment such as that used in mining, construction, and utility industries.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20112" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Heavy Equipment Mechanics" .

ceds:NI001517164395
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Aircraft Power Plant courses provide students with the information necessary
			to troubleshoot, test, repair, and install aircraft engines. Course content usually
			includes engine ignition, electrical, lubrication, cooling, exhaust, and fuel systems,
			along with aircraft instrumentation and safety features.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164395"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Aircraft Power Plant" ;
  skos:definition """Aircraft Power Plant courses provide students with the information
			necessary to troubleshoot, test, repair, and install aircraft engines. Course content
			usually includes engine ignition, electrical, lubrication, cooling, exhaust, and fuel
			systems, along with aircraft instrumentation and safety features.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20113" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Aircraft Power Plant" .

ceds:NI001517164396
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Aircraft Airframe courses offer students information and instruction related
			to the structure and mechanics of aircraft, typically including hydraulic, pneumatic,
			instrumental, fuel, electrical, cabin atmosphere, and landing gear systems. Aircraft
			Airframe courses may also cover aircraft metals and coverings and related welding
			skills.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164396"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Aircraft Airframe" ;
  skos:definition """Aircraft Airframe courses offer students information and instruction
			related to the structure and mechanics of aircraft, typically including hydraulic,
			pneumatic, instrumental, fuel, electrical, cabin atmosphere, and landing gear systems.
			Aircraft Airframe courses may also cover aircraft metals and coverings and related
			welding skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20114" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Aircraft Airframe" .

ceds:NI001517164397
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Automotive Detailing and Reconditioning courses provide students with
			knowledge and skills related to repairing, refinishing, and detailing automobiles.
			Course topics typically include painting and refinishing, plastics and adhesives, damage
			analysis, and repair, in addition to occupational safety, employability, and
			entrepreneurship skills.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164397"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Automotive Detailing and Reconditioning" ;
  skos:definition """Automotive Detailing and Reconditioning courses provide students with
			knowledge and skills related to repairing, refinishing, and detailing automobiles.
			Course topics typically include painting and refinishing, plastics and adhesives, damage
			analysis, and repair, in addition to occupational safety, employability, and
			entrepreneurship skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "20115" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Automotive Detailing and Reconditioning" .

ceds:NI001517164398
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Hybrid Engines courses introduce students to the fundamentals of hybrid
			electric vehicles. These courses explore the hybrid power plant and may include such
			topics as hybrid batteries, high- and low-voltage systems, inverters, safety procedures,
			hybrid maintenance and diagnostics, and alternative fuels.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164398"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Hybrid Engines" ;
  skos:definition """Hybrid Engines courses introduce students to the fundamentals of hybrid
