ceds:NI001517164414
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum, PLTW Introduction to Engineering Design courses provide an opportunity for students to become involved in hands-on projects that require mathematics, science, and engineering applications. In these courses, students review problems, document work in an engineering notebook, and design solutions using 3D modeling software." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164414"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "PLTW Introduction to Engineering Design" ;
  skos:definition "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum, PLTW Introduction to Engineering Design courses provide an opportunity for students to become involved in hands-on projects that require mathematics, science, and engineering applications. In these courses, students review problems, document work in an engineering notebook, and design solutions using 3D modeling software." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21017" ;
  skos:prefLabel "PLTW Introduction to Engineering Design" .

ceds:NI001517164409
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Civil Engineering and Architecture courses provide students with an overview
			of the fields of Civil Engineering and Architecture while emphasizing the
			interrelationship of both fields. Students typically use software to address real world
			problems and to communicate the solutions that they develop. Course topics typically
			include the roles of civil engineers and architects, project-planning, site-planning,
			building design, project documentation, and presentation.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164409"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Civil Engineering and Architecture" ;
  skos:definition """Civil Engineering and Architecture courses provide students with an
