  skos:definition """These courses examine specific topics in engineering other than those
			already described elsewhere in this classification system.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21015" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Engineering" .

ceds:NI001517164413
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Engineering Analysis courses help students apply engineering design
			processes to areas of the designed world, explore ethics in a technological world, and
			examine systems in civil, mechanical, electrical, and chemical engineering. These
			courses may provide STEM-based projects to teach students to communicate information
			through team-based presentations, proposals, and technical reports.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164413"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Engineering Analysis" ;
  skos:definition """Engineering Analysis courses help students apply engineering design
			processes to areas of the designed world, explore ethics in a technological world, and
			examine systems in civil, mechanical, electrical, and chemical engineering. These
			courses may provide STEM-based projects to teach students to communicate information
			through team-based presentations, proposals, and technical reports.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21016" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Engineering Analysis" .

ceds:NI001517164415
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Digital Electronics courses teach students how to use applied logic in the
			development of electronic circuits and devices. Students may use computer simulation
			software to design and test digital circuitry prior to the actual construction of
			circuits and devices.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164415"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Digital Electronics" ;
  skos:definition """Digital Electronics courses teach students how to use applied logic in the
			development of electronic circuits and devices. Students may use computer simulation
			software to design and test digital circuitry prior to the actual construction of
			circuits and devices.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21008" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Digital Electronics" .

ceds:NI001517164416
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Robotics courses help students develop and expand their skills and knowledge
			of robotics and related scientific and engineering topics. Course topics may include
			principles of mechanics, electronics, hydraulics, pneumatics, programmable logic
			controllers. These courses may emphasize the use of engineering principles to design and
			build robots, construct and connect sensors, and program robots in the programming
			language.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164416"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Robotics" ;
  skos:definition """Robotics courses help students develop and expand their skills and
			knowledge of robotics and related scientific and engineering topics. Course topics may
			include principles of mechanics, electronics, hydraulics, pneumatics, programmable logic
			controllers. These courses may emphasize the use of engineering principles to design and
			build robots, construct and connect sensors, and program robots in the programming
			language.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21009" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Robotics" .

ceds:NI001517164417
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Computer Integrated Manufacturing courses involve the study of robotics and
			automation. Building on computer solid modeling skills, students may use computer
			numerical control (CNC) equipment to produce actual models of their three-dimensional
			designs. Course topics may also include fundamental concepts of robotics, automated
			manufacturing, and design analysis.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164417"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Computer Integrated Manufacturing" ;
  skos:definition """Computer Integrated Manufacturing courses involve the study of robotics and
			automation. Building on computer solid modeling skills, students may use computer
			numerical control (CNC) equipment to produce actual models of their three-dimensional
			designs. Course topics may also include fundamental concepts of robotics, automated
			manufacturing, and design analysis.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21010" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Computer Integrated Manufacturing" .

ceds:NI001517164418
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Civil Engineering courses expose students to the concepts and skills used by
			urban planners, developers, and builders. Students may be trained in soil sampling and
			analysis, topography and surveying, and drafting or blueprint-reading. Additional course
			topics may include traffic analysis, geologic principles, and urban design.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164418"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Civil Engineering" ;
  skos:definition """Civil Engineering courses expose students to the concepts and skills used
			by urban planners, developers, and builders. Students may be trained in soil sampling
			and analysis, topography and surveying, and drafting or blueprint-reading. Additional
			course topics may include traffic analysis, geologic principles, and urban design.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21011" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Civil Engineering" .

ceds:NI001517164419
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum and using hands-on activities and simulations, PLTW Environmental Sustainability courses help students investigate and design solutions in response to real-world challenges related to supply and access to drinking water, food supply issues, and renewable energy." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164419"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "PLTW Environmental Sustainability" ;
  skos:definition "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum and using hands-on activities and simulations, PLTW Environmental Sustainability courses help students investigate and design solutions in response to real-world challenges related to supply and access to drinking water, food supply issues, and renewable energy." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21024" ;
  skos:prefLabel "PLTW Environmental Sustainability" .

ceds:NI001517164420
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Laser/Fiber Optics courses cover the history, safety, and theory of laser
			light and laser systems. In these courses, various laser system configurations and
			operations are examined.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164420"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Laser/Fiber Optics" ;
  skos:definition """Laser/Fiber Optics courses cover the history, safety, and theory of laser
			light and laser systems. In these courses, various laser system configurations and
			operations are examined.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21057" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Laser/Fiber Optics" .

ceds:NI001517164421
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Geospatial Technology courses provide students with experiences pertaining
			to the study of geographic information systems (GIS), global positioning systems (GPS),
			remote sensing (RS), digital image processing simulator (DIPS), Geodesy, automated
			cartography (Auto-Carto), land surveying (LS), and navigation. These courses may use
			spatial analysis models and guidelines for integrating, interpreting, analyzing, and
			synthesizing geographic data, with a focus on both the implications and limitations of
			such technologies. Other topics may include interfacing with telecommunications and
			automated database management systems.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164421"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Geospatial Technology" ;
  skos:definition """Geospatial Technology courses provide students with experiences pertaining
			to the study of geographic information systems (GIS), global positioning systems (GPS),
			remote sensing (RS), digital image processing simulator (DIPS), Geodesy, automated
			cartography (Auto-Carto), land surveying (LS), and navigation. These courses may use
			spatial analysis models and guidelines for integrating, interpreting, analyzing, and
			synthesizing geographic data, with a focus on both the implications and limitations of
			such technologies. Other topics may include interfacing with telecommunications and
			automated database management systems.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21058" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Geospatial Technology" .

ceds:NI001517164422
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Modeling and Simulation Technology courses allow students to explore the use
			of modeling, simulation, and game development software to solve real-world problems in
			science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM). These courses typically
			address the systems, processes, tools, and implications of the field of modeling and
			simulation technology. Courses topics may also include evaluating and testing
			engineering designs, modeling geospatial data, observing and analyzing physics
			simulations, programming games for educational purposes, and creating visualization
			systems with 3D models.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164422"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Modeling and Simulation Technology" ;
  skos:definition """Modeling and Simulation Technology courses allow students to explore the
			use of modeling, simulation, and game development software to solve real-world problems
			in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM). These courses typically
			address the systems, processes, tools, and implications of the field of modeling and
			simulation technology. Courses topics may also include evaluating and testing
			engineering designs, modeling geospatial data, observing and analyzing physics
			simulations, programming games for educational purposes, and creating visualization
			systems with 3D models.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21059" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Modeling and Simulation Technology" .

ceds:NI001517164423
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Wind Energy courses introduce students to the terminology and other aspects
			of the wind industry. Course topics may include, but are not limited to, the history and
			development of the wind industry, types and applications of various wind turbines,
			environmental and economic issues of the wind industry, and the future of the industry.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164423"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Wind Energy" ;
  skos:definition """Wind Energy courses introduce students to the terminology and other aspects
			of the wind industry. Course topics may include, but are not limited to, the history and
			development of the wind industry, types and applications of various wind turbines,
			environmental and economic issues of the wind industry, and the future of the industry.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21060" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Wind Energy" .

ceds:NI001517164424
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Wind Turbine Construction and Operation courses provide students with an
			understanding of wind turbine operation and the wind energy industry. These course
			enable students to study site preparation and construction, turbine component
			specifications and manufacturing, operation and maintenance programs, and data
			acquisition and assessment.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164424"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Wind Turbine Construction and Operation" ;
  skos:definition """Wind Turbine Construction and Operation courses provide students with an
			understanding of wind turbine operation and the wind energy industry. These course
			enable students to study site preparation and construction, turbine component
			specifications and manufacturing, operation and maintenance programs, and data
			acquisition and assessment.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21061" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Wind Turbine Construction and Operation" .

ceds:NI001517164425
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """International Baccalaureate (IB) Design, Middle Years Program courses are
			essentially concerned with solving problems, and they encourage students to investigate,
			design, plan, create, and evaluate. Content is balanced among systems, information, and
			materials, but the particular technology subjects may vary. These courses were formerly
			known as IB Technology, Middle Years Program.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164425"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Design, Middle Years Program" ;
  skos:definition """International Baccalaureate (IB) Design, Middle Years Program courses are
			essentially concerned with solving problems, and they encourage students to investigate,
			design, plan, create, and evaluate. Content is balanced among systems, information, and
			materials, but the particular technology subjects may vary. These courses were formerly
			known as IB Technology, Middle Years Program.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21062" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Design, Middle Years Program" .

