ceds:NI001517163440
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB Geography courses prepare students to take the International
			Baccalaureate Geography exams. These courses integrate both physical and human geography
			and explore scientific and socio-economic methodologies and fieldwork. In general, IB
			Geography courses aim to help students understand the relationships within society, the
			relationships between society and the natural environment, and how those relationships
			change over time.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163440"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Geography" ;
  skos:definition """IB Geography courses prepare students to take the International
			Baccalaureate Geography exams. These courses integrate both physical and human geography
			and explore scientific and socio-economic methodologies and fieldwork. In general, IB
			Geography courses aim to help students understand the relationships within society, the
			relationships between society and the natural environment, and how those relationships
			change over time.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04003" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Geography" .

ceds:NI001517163441
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level Human Geography courses, AP Human Geography introduces students to the systematic study of patterns and processes that have shaped the ways in which humans understand, use, and alter the earth's surface. Students use spatial concepts and landscape analysis to examine human social organization and its environmental consequences and also learn about the methods and tools geographers use in their science and practice." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163441"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Human Geography" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level Human Geography courses, AP Human Geography introduces students to the systematic study of patterns and processes that have shaped the ways in which humans understand, use, and alter the earth's surface. Students use spatial concepts and landscape analysis to examine human social organization and its environmental consequences and also learn about the methods and tools geographers use in their science and practice." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04004" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Human Geography" .

