ceds:NI001517163479
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """International Relations courses provide students with an introduction to the
			relationships that exist among nations, including an examination of the modern state;
			the foreign policies of nations; the dynamics of nationalism, ideology, and culture; and
			the role of international organizations. The courses may also emphasize contemporary
			events.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163479"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "International Relations" ;
  skos:definition """International Relations courses provide students with an introduction to
			the relationships that exist among nations, including an examination of the modern
			state; the foreign policies of nations; the dynamics of nationalism, ideology, and
			culture; and the role of international organizations. The courses may also emphasize
			contemporary events.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04155" ;
  skos:prefLabel "International Relations" .

ceds:NI001517163480
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """United States and World Affairs courses provide a study of global
			interrelationships. Topics covered may include geographic, political, economic, and
			social issues of a particular country or region, with an emphasis on how these issues
			influence (or are influenced by) the way in which the United States relates to other
			countries in an interdependent world context.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163480"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "United States and World Affairs" ;
  skos:definition """United States and World Affairs courses provide a study of global
			interrelationships. Topics covered may include geographic, political, economic, and
			social issues of a particular country or region, with an emphasis on how these issues
			influence (or are influenced by) the way in which the United States relates to other
			countries in an interdependent world context.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04156" ;
  skos:prefLabel "United States and World Affairs" .

ceds:NI001517163481
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level U.S. Government and Politics courses, these courses provide students with an analytical perspective on government and politics in the United States, involving both the study of general concepts used to interpret U.S. politics and the analysis of specific case studies and foundational documents. The courses generally cover foundations of American democracy, interaction among branches of government, political beliefs and behaviors, political participation, and civil rights and liberties." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163481"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP U.S. Government and Politics" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level U.S. Government and Politics courses, these courses provide students with an analytical perspective on government and politics in the United States, involving both the study of general concepts used to interpret U.S. politics and the analysis of specific case studies and foundational documents. The courses generally cover foundations of American democracy, interaction among branches of government, political beliefs and behaviors, political participation, and civil rights and liberties." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04157" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP U.S. Government and Politics" .

ceds:NI001517163482
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level Comparative Government and Politics courses, these courses offer students an understanding of the world's diverse political structures and practices. The courses encompass the study of both specific countries and general concepts used to interpret the key political relationships found in virtually all national policies. Course content generally includes sovereignty, authority, and power; political institutions; the relationships among citizens, society, and the state; political and economic change; and public policy." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163482"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Comparative Government and Politics" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level Comparative Government and Politics courses, these courses offer students an understanding of the world's diverse political structures and practices. The courses encompass the study of both specific countries and general concepts used to interpret the key political relationships found in virtually all national policies. Course content generally includes sovereignty, authority, and power; political institutions; the relationships among citizens, society, and the state; political and economic change; and public policy." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04158" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Comparative Government and Politics" .

ceds:NI001517163483
