ceds:NI001517164108
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Biomedical Innovation courses help students apply their knowledge and skills to answer questions or solve problems related to the biomedical sciences. These courses help students design innovative solutions for emerging health challenges and address topics such as clinical medicine, human physiology, medical innovation, water contamination, public health, molecular biology, and forensic autopsy, and public health. These courses may also provide students with the opportunity to work with a mentor or advisor from a university or hospital, physician's office, or industry. Students may design and complete an independent project as part of the course." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164108"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Biomedical Innovation" ;
  skos:definition "Biomedical Innovation courses help students apply their knowledge and skills to answer questions or solve problems related to the biomedical sciences. These courses help students design innovative solutions for emerging health challenges and address topics such as clinical medicine, human physiology, medical innovation, water contamination, public health, molecular biology, and forensic autopsy, and public health. These courses may also provide students with the opportunity to work with a mentor or advisor from a university or hospital, physician's office, or industry. Students may design and complete an independent project as part of the course." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "14255" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Biomedical Innovation" .

