ceds:NI001517164115
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Fire Science courses introduce students to the field of fire prevention and
			control and enable them to extend their knowledge through the use of chemical, physical,
			and engineering principles to understand factors involved in fires. Course topics
			typically include the chemistry of combustion, factors that influence fire (such as
			structural design and meteorology), and safety procedures.""" ;
