  skos:prefLabel "State Test Preparation" .

ceds:NI001517164460
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Seminar courses vary widely, but typically offer a small peer group the
			opportunity to investigate areas of interest. Course objectives may include improvement
			of research and investigatory skills, presentation skills, interpersonal skills, group
			process skills, and problem-solving and critical-thinking skills. Seminars aimed at
			juniors and seniors often include a college and career exploration and planning
			component.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164460"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Seminar" ;
  skos:definition """Seminar courses vary widely, but typically offer a small peer group the
			opportunity to investigate areas of interest. Course objectives may include improvement
			of research and investigatory skills, presentation skills, interpersonal skills, group
			process skills, and problem-solving and critical-thinking skills. Seminars aimed at
			juniors and seniors often include a college and career exploration and planning
			component.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "22106" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Seminar" .

ceds:NI001517164461
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Peer Counseling courses allow students to serve as leaders to reduce
			conflict among their fellow students. Students may work individually or as part of a
			group to solve problems and promote mutual support among their peers.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164461"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Peer Counseling" ;
  skos:definition """Peer Counseling courses allow students to serve as leaders to reduce
			conflict among their fellow students. Students may work individually or as part of a
			group to solve problems and promote mutual support among their peers.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "22107" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Peer Counseling" .

ceds:NI001517164462
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB Creativity, Activity, and Service (CAS) courses are a required
			extracurricular component of the International Baccalaureate program. The CAS
			requirement emphasizes the importance of life outside of the world of scholarship and
			encourages young people to share their energies and special talents while they develop
			awareness, concern, and the ability to work cooperatively with others. Participation in
			theater productions, sports, and community service are examples of activities that
			fulfill the CAS course requirements.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164462"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Creativity, Activity, Service" ;
  skos:definition """IB Creativity, Activity, and Service (CAS) courses are a required
			extracurricular component of the International Baccalaureate program. The CAS
			requirement emphasizes the importance of life outside of the world of scholarship and
			encourages young people to share their energies and special talents while they develop
			awareness, concern, and the ability to work cooperatively with others. Participation in
			theater productions, sports, and community service are examples of activities that
			fulfill the CAS course requirements.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "22108" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Creativity, Activity, Service" .

ceds:NI001517164463
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Obligatory for every International Baccalaureate degree candidate, IB
			Extended Essay aim to help students develop an independent, self-directed piece of
			research, culminating in a 4,000 word paper. These courses provide students with
			practical preparation for later research and help build their analysis, synthesis, and
			evaluation skills.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164463"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Extended Essay" ;
  skos:definition """Obligatory for every International Baccalaureate degree candidate, IB
			Extended Essay aim to help students develop an independent, self-directed piece of
			research, culminating in a 4,000 word paper. These courses provide students with
			practical preparation for later research and help build their analysis, synthesis, and
			evaluation skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "22109" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Extended Essay" .

ceds:NI001517164464
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Study Skills courses prepare students for success in high school and/or for
			postsecondary education. Course topics may vary according to the students involved, but
			typically include reading improvement skills, such as scanning, note-taking, and
			outlining; library and research skills; listening and note-taking; vocabulary skills;
			and test-taking skills. The courses may also include exercises designed to generate
			organized, logical thinking and writing.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164464"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Study Skills" ;
  skos:definition """Study Skills courses prepare students for success in high school and/or for
			postsecondary education. Course topics may vary according to the students involved, but
			typically include reading improvement skills, such as scanning, note-taking, and
			outlining; library and research skills; listening and note-taking; vocabulary skills;
			and test-taking skills. The courses may also include exercises designed to generate
			organized, logical thinking and writing.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "22003" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Study Skills" .

ceds:NI001517164465
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Dropout Prevention Program courses vary widely, but typically are targeted
			at students who have been identified as being at risk of dropping out of or failing in
			school. Course content may include study skills and individual tutorials; career
			exploration or job readiness skills; communication skills; personal assessment and
			awareness activities; speaker presentations; and small-group seminars.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164465"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Dropout Prevention Program" ;
  skos:definition """Dropout Prevention Program courses vary widely, but typically are targeted
			at students who have been identified as being at risk of dropping out of or failing in
			school. Course content may include study skills and individual tutorials; career
			exploration or job readiness skills; communication skills; personal assessment and
			awareness activities; speaker presentations; and small-group seminars.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "22004" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Dropout Prevention Program" .

ceds:NI001517164466
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Tutorial courses provide students with the assistance they need to
			successfully complete their coursework. Students may receive help in one or several
			subjects.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164466"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Tutorial" ;
  skos:definition """Tutorial courses provide students with the assistance they need to
