ceds:NI001517163484
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """U.S. Government, Civics, and Economics courses combine a study of the
			structure of national, state, and local U.S. government with an overview of the
			principles of market economics. Course content may include contemporary U.S. issues.
			These courses prepare students to perform effectively as informed citizens.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163484"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "U.S. Government, Civics, and Economics" ;
  skos:definition """U.S. Government, Civics, and Economics courses combine a study of the
			structure of national, state, and local U.S. government with an overview of the
			principles of market economics. Course content may include contemporary U.S. issues.
			These courses prepare students to perform effectively as informed citizens.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04160" ;
  skos:prefLabel "U.S. Government, Civics, and Economics" .

ceds:NI001517163485
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Civics courses examine the general structure and functions of U.S. systems
			of government, the roles and responsibilities of citizens to participate in the
			political process, and the relationship of the individual to the law and legal system.
			These courses do not typically delve to the same degree of detail into constitutional
			principles or the role of political parties and interest groups as do comprehensive
			courses in U.S. Government.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163485"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Civics" ;
  skos:definition """Civics courses examine the general structure and functions of U.S. systems
			of government, the roles and responsibilities of citizens to participate in the
			political process, and the relationship of the individual to the law and legal system.
			These courses do not typically delve to the same degree of detail into constitutional
			principles or the role of political parties and interest groups as do comprehensive
			courses in U.S. Government.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04161" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Civics" .

ceds:NI001517163486
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Law Studies courses examine the history and philosophy of law as part of
			U.S. society and include the study of the major substantive areas of both criminal and
			civil law, such as constitutional rights, torts, contracts, property, criminal law,
			family law, and equity. Although these courses emphasize the study of law, they may also
			cover the workings of the legal system.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163486"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Law Studies" ;
  skos:definition """Law Studies courses examine the history and philosophy of law as part of
			U.S. society and include the study of the major substantive areas of both criminal and
			civil law, such as constitutional rights, torts, contracts, property, criminal law,
			family law, and equity. Although these courses emphasize the study of law, they may also
			cover the workings of the legal system.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04162" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Law Studies" .

ceds:NI001517163487
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Consumer Law courses present a history and philosophy of law and the legal
			system in the United States, with a particular emphasis on those topics affecting
			students as consumers and young adults (such as contractual laws, laws pertaining to
			housing and marriage, and constitutional rights).""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163487"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Consumer Law" ;
  skos:definition """Consumer Law courses present a history and philosophy of law and the legal
			system in the United States, with a particular emphasis on those topics affecting
			students as consumers and young adults (such as contractual laws, laws pertaining to
			housing and marriage, and constitutional rights).""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04163" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Consumer Law" .

ceds:NI001517163488
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Business Law courses present a history and philosophy of law and the legal
			system in the United States, with a particular emphasis on those topics affecting
			students as future business leaders and employees. Such topics may include contracts,
			commercial paper and debt instruments, property rights, employer/employee relationships,
			and constitutional rights and responsibilities.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163488"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Business Law" ;
  skos:definition """Business Law courses present a history and philosophy of law and the legal
			system in the United States, with a particular emphasis on those topics affecting
			students as future business leaders and employees. Such topics may include contracts,
			commercial paper and debt instruments, property rights, employer/employee relationships,
			and constitutional rights and responsibilities.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04164" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Business Law" .

ceds:NI001517163489
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Government, Politics, and Law—Independent Study courses, often conducted
			with instructors as mentors, enable students to explore topics of interest within one of
			the fields of Government, Politics, and Law. These courses may provide students with an
			opportunity to expand their expertise in a particular specialization, to explore a topic
