ceds:NI001517163500
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Economics courses provide students with an overview of economics with
			primary emphasis on the principles of microeconomics and the U.S. economic system. These
			courses may also cover topics such as principles of macroeconomics, international
			economics, and comparative economics. Economic principles may be presented in formal
			theoretical contexts, applied contexts, or both.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163500"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Economics" ;
  skos:definition """Economics courses provide students with an overview of economics with
			primary emphasis on the principles of microeconomics and the U.S. economic system. These
			courses may also cover topics such as principles of macroeconomics, international
			economics, and comparative economics. Economic principles may be presented in formal
			theoretical contexts, applied contexts, or both.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04201" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Economics" .

ceds:NI001517163501
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Comparative Economics courses offer students an opportunity to study
			different economies and economic systems, including an examination of various approaches
			to problems in micro- and macroeconomics.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163501"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Comparative Economics" ;
  skos:definition """Comparative Economics courses offer students an opportunity to study
			different economies and economic systems, including an examination of various approaches
			to problems in micro- and macroeconomics.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04202" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Comparative Economics" .

ceds:NI001517163502
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level microeconomics, AP Microeconomics courses provide students with a thorough understanding of the principles of economics that apply to the functions of individual decision makers (both consumers and producers). They place primary emphasis on the nature and functions of product markets, while also including a study of factor markets and the role of government in the economy." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163502"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Microeconomics" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level microeconomics, AP Microeconomics courses provide students with a thorough understanding of the principles of economics that apply to the functions of individual decision makers (both consumers and producers). They place primary emphasis on the nature and functions of product markets, while also including a study of factor markets and the role of government in the economy." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04203" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Microeconomics" .

ceds:NI001517163503
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level macroeconomics, AP Macroeconomics courses provide students with a thorough understanding of the principles of economics that apply to an economic system as a whole. They place particular emphasis on the study of national income and price determination and developing students' familiarity with economic performance measures, economic growth, and international economics." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163503"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Macroeconomics" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level macroeconomics, AP Macroeconomics courses provide students with a thorough understanding of the principles of economics that apply to an economic system as a whole. They place particular emphasis on the study of national income and price determination and developing students' familiarity with economic performance measures, economic growth, and international economics." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04204" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Macroeconomics" .

ceds:NI001517163504
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "AP Economics courses prepare students for the College Board's examinations in both AP Microeconomics and AP Macroeconomics. See SCED codes 04203 and 04204 for detailed content descriptions." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163504"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Economics" ;
  skos:definition "AP Economics courses prepare students for the College Board's examinations in both AP Microeconomics and AP Macroeconomics. See SCED codes 04203 and 04204 for detailed content descriptions." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04205" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Economics" .

ceds:NI001517163505
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Economics courses prepare students to take the International Baccalaureate
			Economics exams. The courses provide students with the basic tools of economic reasoning
			and teach them to use those tools to explain or interpret economic problems. Course
			content includes international and development economics, microeconomics, and
			macroeconomics.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163505"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Economics" ;
  skos:definition """Economics courses prepare students to take the International Baccalaureate
			Economics exams. The courses provide students with the basic tools of economic reasoning
			and teach them to use those tools to explain or interpret economic problems. Course
			content includes international and development economics, microeconomics, and
			macroeconomics.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04206" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Economics" .

ceds:NI001517163506
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses examine a particular topic in Economics rather than provide a
			general overview of the field. Course topics may include international economics,
			economic development and growth of a particular country or region, or resource
			allocation.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163506"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Economics" ;
  skos:definition """These courses examine a particular topic in Economics rather than provide a
