ceds:NI001517163835
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Network Technology courses address the technology involved in the
			transmission of data between and among computers through data lines, telephone lines, or
			other transmission media, such as hard wiring, wireless, cable networks, and so on.
			These courses may emphasize the capabilities of networks, network technology itself, or
			both. Students typically learn about network capabilities and network technology,
			including the software, hardware, and peripherals involved in setting up and maintaining
			a computer network.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163835"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Network Technology" ;
  skos:definition """Network Technology courses address the technology involved in the
			transmission of data between and among computers through data lines, telephone lines, or
			other transmission media, such as hard wiring, wireless, cable networks, and so on.
			These courses may emphasize the capabilities of networks, network technology itself, or
			both. Students typically learn about network capabilities and network technology,
			including the software, hardware, and peripherals involved in setting up and maintaining
			a computer network.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10101" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Network Technology" .

ceds:NI001517163836
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum to prepare students for the College Board's Advanced Placement Computer Science A exam, PLTW Computer Science A (formerly known as PLTW Computer Science Applications) courses focus on extending students' computational thinking skills through the use of various industry-standard programming and software tools. In these courses, students collaborate to design and produce solutions to real-life problems." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163836"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "PLTW Computer Science A" ;
  skos:definition "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum to prepare students for the College Board's Advanced Placement Computer Science A exam, PLTW Computer Science A (formerly known as PLTW Computer Science Applications) courses focus on extending students' computational thinking skills through the use of various industry-standard programming and software tools. In these courses, students collaborate to design and produce solutions to real-life problems." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10014" ;
  skos:prefLabel "PLTW Computer Science A" .

ceds:NI001517163837
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum to prepare students for the College Board's Advanced Placement Computer Science Principles exam, PLTW Computer Science Principles (formerly known as PLTW Computer Science and Software Engineering) courses are designed to help students develop computational thinking, and introduce students to possible career paths involving computing. These courses help students build programming expertise and familiarity with the Internet using multiple platforms and programming languages. Course content may include application development, visualization of data, cybersecurity, and simulation." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163837"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "PLTW Computer Science Principles" ;
  skos:definition "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum to prepare students for the College Board's Advanced Placement Computer Science Principles exam, PLTW Computer Science Principles (formerly known as PLTW Computer Science and Software Engineering) courses are designed to help students develop computational thinking, and introduce students to possible career paths involving computing. These courses help students build programming expertise and familiarity with the Internet using multiple platforms and programming languages. Course content may include application development, visualization of data, cybersecurity, and simulation." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10015" ;
  skos:prefLabel "PLTW Computer Science Principles" .

ceds:NI001517163838
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum, PLTW Cybersecurity courses introduce students to the tools and concepts of cybersecurity. In these courses, students are encouraged to understand vulnerabilities in computational resources and to create solutions that allow people to share computing resources while retaining privacy. These courses also introduce students to issues related to ethical computing behavior." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163838"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "PLTW Cybersecurity" ;
  skos:definition "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum, PLTW Cybersecurity courses introduce students to the tools and concepts of cybersecurity. In these courses, students are encouraged to understand vulnerabilities in computational resources and to create solutions that allow people to share computing resources while retaining privacy. These courses also introduce students to issues related to ethical computing behavior." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10016" ;
  skos:prefLabel "PLTW Cybersecurity" .

ceds:NI001517163839
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level computer science principles courses, AP Computer Science Principles courses introduce students to the fundamental ideas of computer science and how to apply computational thinking across multiple disciplines. These courses teach students to apply creative designs and innovative solutions when developing computational artifacts. These courses cover such topics as creative development, data, algorithms and programming, computer systems and networks, and the impact of computing." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163839"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Computer Science Principles" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level computer science principles courses, AP Computer Science Principles courses introduce students to the fundamental ideas of computer science and how to apply computational thinking across multiple disciplines. These courses teach students to apply creative designs and innovative solutions when developing computational artifacts. These courses cover such topics as creative development, data, algorithms and programming, computer systems and networks, and the impact of computing." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10019" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Computer Science Principles" .

ceds:NI001517164135
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Nutrition and Food Preparation courses provide students with knowledge and
			skills related to commercial food preparation and/or production, with a strong emphasis
			on nutrition, balanced diets, and satisfying special dietary needs. Topics typically
			include assessing nutrient content, the science of food and nutrition, physiology and
			utilization of nutrients. Course content may also cover additives, contaminants, food-
			borne illnesses, and food technology.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164135"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Nutrition and Food Preparation" ;
  skos:definition """Nutrition and Food Preparation courses provide students with knowledge and
			skills related to commercial food preparation and/or production, with a strong emphasis
			on nutrition, balanced diets, and satisfying special dietary needs. Topics typically
			include assessing nutrient content, the science of food and nutrition, physiology and
			utilization of nutrients. Course content may also cover additives, contaminants, food-
