ceds:NI001517164149
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Exploration of Manufacturing Occupations courses introduce and expose
			students to the career opportunities pertaining to the processing and production of
			goods. Course topics vary and may include (but are not limited to) systems pertinent to
			the manufacturing process, properties of various raw materials, and the methods used to
			transform materials into consumer products. Course activities depend upon the careers
			being explored; course topics may include entrepreneurship, labor laws, economic impact,
			and customer service.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164149"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Exploration of Manufacturing Occupations" ;
  skos:definition """Exploration of Manufacturing Occupations courses introduce and expose
			students to the career opportunities pertaining to the processing and production of
			goods. Course topics vary and may include (but are not limited to) systems pertinent to
			the manufacturing process, properties of various raw materials, and the methods used to
			transform materials into consumer products. Course activities depend upon the careers
			being explored; course topics may include entrepreneurship, labor laws, economic impact,
			and customer service.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13001" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Exploration of Manufacturing Occupations" .

ceds:NI001517164150
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Manufacturing—Comprehensive courses introduce students to the various
			methods used to process and transform materials. Processing techniques covered usually
			include casting, forming, separating, assembling, and finishing. The courses may also
			include an overview of management techniques in planning, organizing, and controlling
			various segments of the manufacturing process, including design, automation,
			engineering, production, and marketing.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164150"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Manufacturing—Comprehensive" ;
  skos:definition """Manufacturing—Comprehensive courses introduce students to the various
			methods used to process and transform materials. Processing techniques covered usually
			include casting, forming, separating, assembling, and finishing. The courses may also
			include an overview of management techniques in planning, organizing, and controlling
			various segments of the manufacturing process, including design, automation,
			engineering, production, and marketing.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13002" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Manufacturing—Comprehensive" .

ceds:NI001517164151
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Industrial Arts courses expose students to the tools and equipment that they
			may encounter in manufacturing-related occupations and enable them to develop the skills
			they need to use these tools in various applications. Course topics typically include
			(but are not limited to) planning and design, electricity and electronics, materials
			properties and testing, basic materials processing, and power technology. These courses
			typically cover general safety and career exploration as well.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164151"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Industrial Arts" ;
  skos:definition """Industrial Arts courses expose students to the tools and equipment that
			they may encounter in manufacturing-related occupations and enable them to develop the
			skills they need to use these tools in various applications. Course topics typically
			include (but are not limited to) planning and design, electricity and electronics,
			materials properties and testing, basic materials processing, and power technology.
			These courses typically cover general safety and career exploration as well.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13003" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Industrial Arts" .

ceds:NI001517164152
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Industrial Safety/First Aid courses immerse students in the study of safe
			operating procedures related to various industrial environments, as well as more general
			training in emergency first aid and CPR. Course topics may include the importance of
			standard operation procedures, appropriate use of equipment, agencies and regulations
			related to occupational safety and hazard prevention, and the dangers of particular
			materials.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164152"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Industrial Safety/First Aid" ;
  skos:definition """Industrial Safety/First Aid courses immerse students in the study of safe
			operating procedures related to various industrial environments, as well as more general
			training in emergency first aid and CPR. Course topics may include the importance of
			standard operation procedures, appropriate use of equipment, agencies and regulations
			related to occupational safety and hazard prevention, and the dangers of particular
			materials.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13004" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Industrial Safety/First Aid" .

ceds:NI001517164153
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Material and Processes courses expose students to the tools, equipment, and
			processes that may be encountered in manufacturing-related occupations. In particular,
			these courses stress the analysis, testing, and processing of metals, plastics, woods,
			ceramics, and composite materials.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164153"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Material and Processes" ;
  skos:definition """Material and Processes courses expose students to the tools, equipment, and
			processes that may be encountered in manufacturing-related occupations. In particular,
			these courses stress the analysis, testing, and processing of metals, plastics, woods,
			ceramics, and composite materials.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13052" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Material and Processes" .

ceds:NI001517164154
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Metal and Wood Processing/Production courses allow students to study the
			physical and chemical properties of metals, woods, and composites and to use these
			materials to construct usable products according to industry standards. These courses
			enable students to experience the process of translating an idea into a finished
			product, with instruction in planning, designing, selecting materials, and using tools
			and machines.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164154"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Metal and Wood Processing/Production" ;
  skos:definition """Metal and Wood Processing/Production courses allow students to study the
