ceds:NI001517164483
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches courses prepare students to take the
			International Baccalaureate Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches exams. These courses
			prepare students to use analytical concepts within mathematics to solve abstract
			problems in a variety of contexts. These concepts are applied to course topics such as
			numbers and algebra, functions, geometry and trigonometry, statistics and probability,
			and calculus.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164483"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches" ;
  skos:definition """IB Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches courses prepare students to take
			the International Baccalaureate Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches exams. These
			courses prepare students to use analytical concepts within mathematics to solve abstract
			problems in a variety of contexts. These concepts are applied to course topics such as
			numbers and algebra, functions, geometry and trigonometry, statistics and probability,
			and calculus.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "02140" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches" .

ceds:NI001517164484
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum, PLTW Biomedical Innovation courses help students apply their knowledge and skills to design innovative solutions related to biomedical challenges. These courses address topics ranging from public health and biomedical engineering to clinical medicine and physiology. Theses courses may also provide students with the opportunity to work with a mentor or advisor from a university, medical facility, or research institution. Students may design and complete an independent project as part of the course." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164484"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "PLTW Biomedical Innovation" ;
  skos:definition "Following Project Lead the Way's suggested curriculum, PLTW Biomedical Innovation courses help students apply their knowledge and skills to design innovative solutions related to biomedical challenges. These courses address topics ranging from public health and biomedical engineering to clinical medicine and physiology. Theses courses may also provide students with the opportunity to work with a mentor or advisor from a university, medical facility, or research institution. Students may design and complete an independent project as part of the course." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "03070" ;
  skos:prefLabel "PLTW Biomedical Innovation" .

ceds:NI001517164485
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level World History courses, AP World History: Modern courses examine world history from 1200 CE to the present with the aim of helping students make connections of historical evolution across times and places. These courses highlight the interaction between humans and the environment; development and interaction of cultures; state-building, expansion and conflict; creation, expansion and interaction of economic systems; development and transformation of social structures; and technology and innovation." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164485"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP World History: Modern" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level World History courses, AP World History: Modern courses examine world history from 1200 CE to the present with the aim of helping students make connections of historical evolution across times and places. These courses highlight the interaction between humans and the environment; development and interaction of cultures; state-building, expansion and conflict; creation, expansion and interaction of economic systems; development and transformation of social structures; and technology and innovation." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "04067" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP World History: Modern" .

