  rdfs:label "Language Arts (grade 6)" ;
  skos:definition "Language Arts (grade 6) courses build upon students' prior knowledge of grammar, vocabulary, word usage, and the mechanics of writing, and include the four aspects of language use: reading, writing, speaking, and listening. These courses may emphasize the use of language for different effects, in different contexts, and for different purposes. Specific content depends upon state standards for grade 6." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "01034" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Language Arts (grade 6)" .

ceds:NI001517163190
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Language Arts (grade 7) courses build upon students' prior knowledge of grammar, vocabulary, word usage, and the mechanics of writing, and include the four aspects of language use: reading, writing, speaking, and listening. Beyond emphasizing different uses for language, these courses may also include using language (particularly written text) to construct meaning and connections. Specific content depends upon state standards for grade 7." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163190"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Language Arts (grade 7)" ;
  skos:definition "Language Arts (grade 7) courses build upon students' prior knowledge of grammar, vocabulary, word usage, and the mechanics of writing, and include the four aspects of language use: reading, writing, speaking, and listening. Beyond emphasizing different uses for language, these courses may also include using language (particularly written text) to construct meaning and connections. Specific content depends upon state standards for grade 7." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "01035" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Language Arts (grade 7)" .

ceds:NI001517163191
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Language Arts (grade 8) courses build upon students' prior knowledge of grammar, vocabulary, word usage, and the mechanics of writing, and include the four aspects of language use: reading, writing, speaking, and listening. Typically, these courses use various genres of literature to improve reading skills, and they link writing exercises for different purposes to those reading selections. Specific content depends upon state standards for grade 8." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163191"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Language Arts (grade 8)" ;
  skos:definition "Language Arts (grade 8) courses build upon students' prior knowledge of grammar, vocabulary, word usage, and the mechanics of writing, and include the four aspects of language use: reading, writing, speaking, and listening. Typically, these courses use various genres of literature to improve reading skills, and they link writing exercises for different purposes to those reading selections. Specific content depends upon state standards for grade 8." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "01036" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Language Arts (grade 8)" .

