ceds:NI001517163840
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Computer Literacy—Independent Study courses, often conducted with
			instructors as mentors, enable students to explore computer-related topics of interest.
			Independent Study courses may serve as an opportunity for students to expand their
			expertise in a particular specialization, to explore a topic in greater detail, or to
			develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163840"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Computer Literacy—Independent Study" ;
  skos:definition """Computer Literacy—Independent Study courses, often conducted with
			instructors as mentors, enable students to explore computer-related topics of interest.
			Independent Study courses may serve as an opportunity for students to expand their
			expertise in a particular specialization, to explore a topic in greater detail, or to
			develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10047" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Computer Literacy—Independent Study" .

ceds:NI001517163841
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Computer Literacy—Workplace Experience courses provide work experience in
			fields related to computer literacy. Goals are typically set cooperatively by the
			student, teacher, and employer (although students are not necessarily paid). These
			courses may include classroom activities as well, involving further study of the field
			or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter in the workplace.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163841"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Computer Literacy—Workplace Experience" ;
  skos:definition """Computer Literacy—Workplace Experience courses provide work experience in
			fields related to computer literacy. Goals are typically set cooperatively by the
			student, teacher, and employer (although students are not necessarily paid). These
			courses may include classroom activities as well, involving further study of the field
			or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter in the workplace.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10048" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Computer Literacy—Workplace Experience" .

ceds:NI001517163842
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Computer and Information Technology courses teach students to operate and
			use computer and information technology, emphasizing their role as tools to communicate
			more effectively, conduct research more efficiently, and increase productivity. Course
			content includes the legal and ethical issues involved with computer technology and use.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163842"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Computer and Information Technology" ;
  skos:definition """Computer and Information Technology courses teach students to operate and
			use computer and information technology, emphasizing their role as tools to communicate
			more effectively, conduct research more efficiently, and increase productivity. Course
			content includes the legal and ethical issues involved with computer technology and use.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10003" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Computer and Information Technology" .

ceds:NI001517163843
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """In Computer Applications courses, students acquire knowledge of and
			experience in the proper and efficient use of previously written software packages.
			These courses explore a wide range of applications, including (but not limited to)
			word-processing, spreadsheet, presentation, graphics, and database programs. Courses may
			also cover the use of electronic mail and online collaborative software.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163843"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Computer Applications" ;
  skos:definition """In Computer Applications courses, students acquire knowledge of and
			experience in the proper and efficient use of previously written software packages.
			These courses explore a wide range of applications, including (but not limited to)
			word-processing, spreadsheet, presentation, graphics, and database programs. Courses may
			also cover the use of electronic mail and online collaborative software.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10004" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Computer Applications" .

ceds:NI001517163844
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """In Business Computer Applications courses, students expand their knowledge
			of and experience in the proper and efficient use of previously written software
			packages, particularly those used in business. Generally, these courses explore a wide
			range of applications including (but not limited to) word processing, spreadsheet,
			presentation, graphics, and database programs, and they may also cover topics such as
			electronic mail, desktop publishing, and telecommunications. Advanced topics may include
			integrated software applications, including printed, electronic, and Web publications;
			computer maintenance activities; and Web site development.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163844"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Business Computer Applications" ;
  skos:definition """In Business Computer Applications courses, students expand their knowledge
			of and experience in the proper and efficient use of previously written software
			packages, particularly those used in business. Generally, these courses explore a wide
			range of applications including (but not limited to) word processing, spreadsheet,
			presentation, graphics, and database programs, and they may also cover topics such as
			electronic mail, desktop publishing, and telecommunications. Advanced topics may include
			integrated software applications, including printed, electronic, and Web publications;
			computer maintenance activities; and Web site development.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10005" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Business Computer Applications" .

ceds:NI001517163845
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Telecommunications courses address the growth in global communications and
			the emerging equipment and systems needed to successfully communicate in a global
			environment. These courses cover such topics as data communication protocol and systems,
			government regulations of the communications industry, the use of cost-effective and
			productive tools to transmit messages and data, and live synchronistic video exchanges.
			Other topics may include telecommunications terminology, tools and test equipment;
			customer service experience; and installation, repair, and delivery of
			telecommunications systems. In these courses, students may learn about such
			communication systems as e-mail, internet, or e-commerce, local area network (LAN), wide
			area network (WAN), voice transmission, cell phone technology, teleconferencing, and
			videoconferencing.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163845"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Telecommunications" ;
  skos:definition """Telecommunications courses address the growth in global communications and
			the emerging equipment and systems needed to successfully communicate in a global
			environment. These courses cover such topics as data communication protocol and systems,
			government regulations of the communications industry, the use of cost-effective and
			productive tools to transmit messages and data, and live synchronistic video exchanges.
			Other topics may include telecommunications terminology, tools and test equipment;
			customer service experience; and installation, repair, and delivery of
			telecommunications systems. In these courses, students may learn about such
			communication systems as e-mail, internet, or e-commerce, local area network (LAN), wide
			area network (WAN), voice transmission, cell phone technology, teleconferencing, and
			videoconferencing.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10006" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Telecommunications" .

ceds:NI001517163846
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB Digital Society courses prepare students to take the International
			Baccalaureate Digital Society exams and examine the interaction among information,
			technology, and society. Course content is designed to help students develop a
			systematic, problem solving approach to processing and analyzing information using a
			range of information tools. In these courses, students also discuss and evaluate how
			modern information technology affects individuals, relationships among people, and
			institutions and societies. This course is also called IB Information Technology in a
			Global Society.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163846"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Digital Society" ;
  skos:definition """IB Digital Society courses prepare students to take the International
			Baccalaureate Digital Society exams and examine the interaction among information,
			technology, and society. Course content is designed to help students develop a
			systematic, problem solving approach to processing and analyzing information using a
			range of information tools. In these courses, students also discuss and evaluate how
			modern information technology affects individuals, relationships among people, and
			institutions and societies. This course is also called IB Information Technology in a
			Global Society.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10007" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Digital Society" .

ceds:NI001517163847
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses examine particular topics related to general computer literacy
			other than those already described elsewhere in this classification system, such as
			privacy issues or instruction in using a particular software application.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163847"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Computer Literacy" ;
  skos:definition """These courses examine particular topics related to general computer
			literacy other than those already described elsewhere in this classification system,
			such as privacy issues or instruction in using a particular software application.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10008" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Computer Literacy" .

ceds:NI001517163848
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Internet Skills courses introduce students to the World Wide Web and the
			Internet. Course content may include search techniques and algorithms, web browser
			utilization, website creation, and the history of the Internet.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163848"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Internet Skills" ;
  skos:definition """Internet Skills courses introduce students to the World Wide Web and the
			Internet. Course content may include search techniques and algorithms, web browser
			utilization, website creation, and the history of the Internet.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10009" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Internet Skills" .

ceds:NI001517163854
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """NetWare Routing courses introduce students to such topics as Virtual LANs
			(VLAN) and switched internetworking, comparing traditional shared local area network
			(LAN) configurations with switched LAN configurations, and they also discuss the
			benefits of using a switched VLAN architecture. These courses also may cover routing
			protocols like RIP, IGRP, Novell IPX, and Access Control Lists (ACLs).""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163854"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "NetWare Routing" ;
  skos:definition """NetWare Routing courses introduce students to such topics as Virtual LANs
			(VLAN) and switched internetworking, comparing traditional shared local area network
			(LAN) configurations with switched LAN configurations, and they also discuss the
			benefits of using a switched VLAN architecture. These courses also may cover routing
			protocols like RIP, IGRP, Novell IPX, and Access Control Lists (ACLs).""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10105" ;
  skos:prefLabel "NetWare Routing" .

ceds:NI001517163849
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Computer Science Principles courses provide students the opportunity use
			programming, computational thinking, and data analytics to create digital artifacts and
			documents representing design and analysis in areas including the Internet, algorithms,
			and the impact that these have on science, business, and society. Computer Science
			Principles courses teach students to use computational tools and techniques including
			abstraction, modeling, and simulation to collaborate in solving problems that connect
			computation to their lives.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163849"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Computer Science Principles" ;
  skos:definition """Computer Science Principles courses provide students the opportunity use
			programming, computational thinking, and data analytics to create digital artifacts and
			documents representing design and analysis in areas including the Internet, algorithms,
			and the impact that these have on science, business, and society. Computer Science
			Principles courses teach students to use computational tools and techniques including
			abstraction, modeling, and simulation to collaborate in solving problems that connect
			computation to their lives.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10011" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Computer Science Principles" .

ceds:NI001517163850
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Exploring Computer Science courses present students with the conceptual
			underpinnings of computer science through an exploration of human computer interaction,
			web design, computer programming, data modeling, and robotics. While these courses
			include programming, the focus is on the computational practices associated with doing
			computer science, rather than just a narrow focus on coding, syntax, or tools. Exploring
			Computer Science courses teach students the computational practices of algorithm design,
			problem solving, and programming within a context that is relevant to their lives.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163850"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Exploring Computer Science" ;
  skos:definition """Exploring Computer Science courses present students with the conceptual
			underpinnings of computer science through an exploration of human computer interaction,
			web design, computer programming, data modeling, and robotics. While these courses
			include programming, the focus is on the computational practices associated with doing
			computer science, rather than just a narrow focus on coding, syntax, or tools. Exploring
			Computer Science courses teach students the computational practices of algorithm design,
			problem solving, and programming within a context that is relevant to their lives.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10012" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Exploring Computer Science" .

ceds:NI001517163851
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Networking Systems courses are designed to provide students with the
			opportunity to understand and work with hubs, switches, and routers. Students develop an
			understanding of LAN (local area network), WAN (wide area network), wireless
			connectivity, and Internet-based communications (including cloud-based computing), with
			a strong emphasis on network function, design, and installation practices. Students
			acquire skills in the design, installation, maintenance, and management of network
			systems that may help them obtain network certification.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163851"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Networking Systems" ;
  skos:definition """Networking Systems courses are designed to provide students with the
			opportunity to understand and work with hubs, switches, and routers. Students develop an
			understanding of LAN (local area network), WAN (wide area network), wireless
			connectivity, and Internet-based communications (including cloud-based computing), with
			a strong emphasis on network function, design, and installation practices. Students
			acquire skills in the design, installation, maintenance, and management of network
			systems that may help them obtain network certification.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10102" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Networking Systems" .

ceds:NI001517163852
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Area Network Design and Protocols courses address the role of computers in a
			network system, the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model, structured wiring systems,
			and simple LAN (local area network) and WAN (wide area network) designs.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163852"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Area Network Design and Protocols" ;
  skos:definition """Area Network Design and Protocols courses address the role of computers in
			a network system, the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model, structured wiring
			systems, and simple LAN (local area network) and WAN (wide area network) designs.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10103" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Area Network Design and Protocols" .

ceds:NI001517163853
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Router Basics courses teach students about router components, installation,
			and configuration using routers (e.g., CISCO) switches and the IOS (Internetwork
			Operation System). These courses also cover such topics as TCP/IP protocol, IP
			addressing, subnetting concepts, and network trouble-shooting.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163853"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Router Basics" ;
  skos:definition """Router Basics courses teach students about router components, installation,
			and configuration using routers (e.g., CISCO) switches and the IOS (Internetwork
			Operation System). These courses also cover such topics as TCP/IP protocol, IP
			addressing, subnetting concepts, and network trouble-shooting.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10104" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Router Basics" .

ceds:NI001517163855
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Wide Area Telecommunications and Networking courses provide students with
			the knowledge and skills to enable them to design Wide Area Networks (WANs) using ISDN,
			Frame-Relay, and PPP. These courses provide students with an understanding of
			internetworking and expertise in trouble-shooting and assessing the adequacy of network
			configurations to meet changing conditions. Topics may include also Local Area Network
			(LAN) segmentation.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163855"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Wide Area Telecommunications and Networking" ;
  skos:definition """Wide Area Telecommunications and Networking courses provide students with
			the knowledge and skills to enable them to design Wide Area Networks (WANs) using ISDN,
			Frame-Relay, and PPP. These courses provide students with an understanding of
			internetworking and expertise in trouble-shooting and assessing the adequacy of network
			configurations to meet changing conditions. Topics may include also Local Area Network
			(LAN) segmentation.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10106" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Wide Area Telecommunications and Networking" .

ceds:NI001517163856
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Wireless Networks courses focus on the design, planning, implementation,
			operation, and trouble-shooting of wireless computer networks, including local access
			networks (LANs). These courses typically include a comprehensive overview of best
			practices in technology, security, and design.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163856"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Wireless Networks" ;
  skos:definition """Wireless Networks courses focus on the design, planning, implementation,
			operation, and trouble-shooting of wireless computer networks, including local access
			networks (LANs). These courses typically include a comprehensive overview of best
			practices in technology, security, and design.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10107" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Wireless Networks" .

ceds:NI001517163857
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Network Security courses provide students with an understanding of network
			security principles and implementation. Course topics usually include authentication,
			the types of attacks and malicious code that may be used against computer networks, the
			threats and countermeasures for e-mail, Web applications, remote access, and file and
			print services. These courses may also cover a variety of security topologies as well as
			technologies and concepts used for providing secure communication channels, secure
			internetworking devices, intrusion detection systems, and firewalls.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163857"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Network Security" ;
  skos:definition """Network Security courses provide students with an understanding of network
			security principles and implementation. Course topics usually include authentication,
			the types of attacks and malicious code that may be used against computer networks, the
			threats and countermeasures for e-mail, Web applications, remote access, and file and
			print services. These courses may also cover a variety of security topologies as well as
			technologies and concepts used for providing secure communication channels, secure
			internetworking devices, intrusion detection systems, and firewalls.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10108" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Network Security" .

ceds:NI001517163858
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Marine Corps Junior Reserve Officer Training Corps (ROTC) II courses build
			upon Marine Corps Junior ROTC I. These courses emphasize personal growth and
			responsibility, leadership, and citizenship along with military subjects that typically
			include the mission, organization, and history of the Marine Corps; geography, maps, and
			navigation; drill and ceremony; and military justice. Students learn about such
			leadership skills as authority, responsibility, and accountability and citizenship
			topics including U.S. government structures, documents, and symbols.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163858"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Marine Corps Junior ROTC II" ;
  skos:definition """Marine Corps Junior Reserve Officer Training Corps (ROTC) II courses build
			upon Marine Corps Junior ROTC I. These courses emphasize personal growth and
			responsibility, leadership, and citizenship along with military subjects that typically
			include the mission, organization, and history of the Marine Corps; geography, maps, and
			navigation; drill and ceremony; and military justice. Students learn about such
			leadership skills as authority, responsibility, and accountability and citizenship
			topics including U.S. government structures, documents, and symbols.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "09202" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Marine Corps Junior ROTC II" .

ceds:NI001517163864
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Other Military Sciences courses." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163864"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Military Science—Other" ;
  skos:definition "Other Military Sciences courses." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "09999" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Military Science—Other" .

ceds:NI001517163859
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Marine Corps Junior Reserve Officer Training Corps (ROTC) III courses build
			upon prior Marine Corps Junior ROTC courses. These courses include (but are not limited
			to) leadership practice, including training, inspection and evaluation; public service
			career opportunities; and citizenship responsibilities. These courses cover such
			personal skills as financial planning, saving and investing, and evaluating credit and
			insurance terms. Students learn about the structures of other armed service branches,
			advance their mapping and navigation skills, and may study firearm use, safety and
			marksmanship. Students continue to learn teamwork, Marine Corps history, and military
			principles.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163859"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Marine Corps Junior ROTC III" ;
  skos:definition """Marine Corps Junior Reserve Officer Training Corps (ROTC) III courses build
			upon prior Marine Corps Junior ROTC courses. These courses include (but are not limited
			to) leadership practice, including training, inspection and evaluation; public service
			career opportunities; and citizenship responsibilities. These courses cover such
			personal skills as financial planning, saving and investing, and evaluating credit and
			insurance terms. Students learn about the structures of other armed service branches,
			advance their mapping and navigation skills, and may study firearm use, safety and
			marksmanship. Students continue to learn teamwork, Marine Corps history, and military
			principles.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "09203" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Marine Corps Junior ROTC III" .

ceds:NI001517163860
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Marine Corps Junior Reserve Officer Training Corps (ROTC) IV courses focus
			on the practical application of skills learned throughout the program: leadership,
			communication (written and verbal), personal growth, and public service. These courses
			emphasize drill and ceremony, physical fitness, marksmanship, land navigation, and
			military history at more advanced levels than in previous courses.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163860"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Marine Corps Junior ROTC IV" ;
  skos:definition """Marine Corps Junior Reserve Officer Training Corps (ROTC) IV courses focus
			on the practical application of skills learned throughout the program: leadership,
			communication (written and verbal), personal growth, and public service. These courses
			emphasize drill and ceremony, physical fitness, marksmanship, land navigation, and
			military history at more advanced levels than in previous courses.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "09204" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Marine Corps Junior ROTC IV" .

ceds:NI001517163861
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Military Science—Aide courses offer students the opportunity to assist
			instructors in preparing, organizing, or delivering course curricula. Students may
			provide tutorial or instructional assistance to other students.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163861"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Military Science—Aide" ;
  skos:definition """Military Science—Aide courses offer students the opportunity to assist
			instructors in preparing, organizing, or delivering course curricula. Students may
			provide tutorial or instructional assistance to other students.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "09995" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Military Science—Aide" .

ceds:NI001517163862
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Courses in Military Science—Independent Study, often conducted with
			instructors/armed services personnel as mentors, enable students to explore topics of
			interest related to military science. Independent Study courses may serve as an
			opportunity for students to expand their expertise in a particular application, to
			explore a topic in greater detail, or to develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163862"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Military Science—Independent Study" ;
  skos:definition """Courses in Military Science—Independent Study, often conducted with
			instructors/armed services personnel as mentors, enable students to explore topics of
			interest related to military science. Independent Study courses may serve as an
			opportunity for students to expand their expertise in a particular application, to
			explore a topic in greater detail, or to develop more advanced skills.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "09997" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Military Science—Independent Study" .

ceds:NI001517163863
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Military Science—Workplace Experience courses provide students with work
			experience within the field of military science and are supported by classroom
			attendance and discussion. In these courses, goals are set for the employment period,
			and classroom experience may involve further study in the field, improvement of
			employability skills, or discussion regarding the experiences and problems that students
			encounter on the job.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163863"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Military Science—Workplace Experience" ;
  skos:definition """Military Science—Workplace Experience courses provide students with work
			experience within the field of military science and are supported by classroom
			attendance and discussion. In these courses, goals are set for the employment period,
			and classroom experience may involve further study in the field, improvement of
			employability skills, or discussion regarding the experiences and problems that students
			encounter on the job.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "09998" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Military Science—Workplace Experience" .

ceds:NI001517163865
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Formerly known as Introduction to Computers, Introduction to Computer Technology courses introduce students to computers, including peripheral and mobile devices; the functions and uses of computer technology; the language used in the industry; possible applications of various computer-based technologies; and occupations related to computer technology hardware and software industries. These courses typically explore legal and ethical issues associated with computer technology use, as well as how changes influence modern society. Students may also be required to perform some computer technology operations." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163865"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Introduction to Computer Technology" ;
  skos:definition """Formerly known as Introduction to Computers, Introduction to Computer Technology courses introduce students to computers, including peripheral and mobile devices; the functions and uses of computer technology; the language used in the industry; possible applications of various computer-based technologies; and occupations related to computer technology hardware and software industries. These courses typically explore legal and ethical issues associated with computer technology use, as well as how changes influence modern society. Students may also be required to perform some computer technology operations.
		""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10001" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Introduction to Computer Technology" .

ceds:NI001517163866
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Computing Systems courses offer a broad exploration of the use of computers
			in a variety of fields. These courses have a considerable range of content, but
			typically include the introduction of robotics and control systems, computer-assisted
			design, computer-aided manufacturing systems, and other computer technologies as they
			relate to industry applications.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163866"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Computing Systems" ;
  skos:definition """Computing Systems courses offer a broad exploration of the use of computers
			in a variety of fields. These courses have a considerable range of content, but
			typically include the introduction of robotics and control systems, computer-assisted
			design, computer-aided manufacturing systems, and other computer technologies as they
			relate to industry applications.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10002" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Computing Systems" .

ceds:NI001517163867
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Essentials of Network Operating Systems courses provide students with an overview of multi-user, multi-tasking network operating systems. In these courses, students study the characteristics of operating systems, such as Linux, and various Windows network operating systems and explore a range of topics including installation procedures, security issues, back-up procedures, and remote access. Advanced topics may include network administration, including account management, training, evaluating new technology, developing system policies, troubleshooting, e-mail and business communications and Web site management." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163867"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Essentials of Network Operating Systems" ;
  skos:definition """Essentials of Network Operating Systems courses provide students with an overview of multi-user, multi-tasking network operating systems. In these courses, students study the characteristics of operating systems, such as Linux, and various Windows network operating systems and explore a range of topics including installation procedures, security issues, back-up procedures, and remote access. Advanced topics may include network administration, including account management, training, evaluating new technology, developing system policies, troubleshooting, e-mail and business communications and Web site management.

		""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10109" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Essentials of Network Operating Systems" .

ceds:NI001517163868
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Visual Basic (VB) Programming courses provide an opportunity for students to
			gain expertise in computer programs using the Visual Basic (VB) language. As with more
			general computer programming courses, the emphasis is on how to structure and document
			computer programs and how to use problem-solving techniques. These courses cover such
			topics as the use of text boxes, scroll bars, menus, buttons, and Windows applications.
			More advanced topics may include mathematical and business functions and graphics.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163868"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Visual Basic (VB) Programming" ;
  skos:definition """Visual Basic (VB) Programming courses provide an opportunity for students
			to gain expertise in computer programs using the Visual Basic (VB) language. As with
			more general computer programming courses, the emphasis is on how to structure and
			document computer programs and how to use problem-solving techniques. These courses
			cover such topics as the use of text boxes, scroll bars, menus, buttons, and Windows
			applications. More advanced topics may include mathematical and business functions and
			graphics.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10153" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Visual Basic (VB) Programming" .

ceds:NI001517163869
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Media Technology—Workplace Experience courses provide students with work
			experience in fields related to media technology. Goals are typically set cooperatively
			by the student, teacher, and employer (although students are not necessarily paid).
			These courses may include classroom activities as well, involving further study of the
			field or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter in the workplace.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163869"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Media Technology—Workplace Experience" ;
  skos:definition """Media Technology—Workplace Experience courses provide students with work
			experience in fields related to media technology. Goals are typically set cooperatively
			by the student, teacher, and employer (although students are not necessarily paid).
			These courses may include classroom activities as well, involving further study of the
			field or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter in the workplace.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "10248" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Media Technology—Workplace Experience" .

ceds:NI001517163870
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Other Media Technology courses." ;
