			such as floor framing, wall and partition framing, interior finishing, or exterior
			finishing.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17005" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Carpentry" .

ceds:NI001517164199
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Woodworking courses introduce students to the various kinds of woods used in
			industry and offer experience in using selected woodworking tools. Students design and
			construct one or more projects and may prepare a bill of materials. Correct and safe use
			of tools and equipment is emphasized. As students advance, they focus on learning the
			terminology necessary to use power tools successfully, developing skills to safely use
			these tools in the workshop and becoming familiar with various kinds of wood-finishing
			materials. Advanced students typically design a project, prepare bills of materials,
			construct, and finish proposed projects.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164199"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Woodworking" ;
  skos:definition """Woodworking courses introduce students to the various kinds of woods used
			in industry and offer experience in using selected woodworking tools. Students design
			and construct one or more projects and may prepare a bill of materials. Correct and safe
			use of tools and equipment is emphasized. As students advance, they focus on learning
			the terminology necessary to use power tools successfully, developing skills to safely
			use these tools in the workshop and becoming familiar with various kinds of
			wood-finishing materials. Advanced students typically design a project, prepare bills of
			materials, construct, and finish proposed projects.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17006" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Woodworking" .

ceds:NI001517164200
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Cabinetmaking courses provide students with experience in constructing
			cases, cabinets, counters, and other interior woodwork. Students learn to distinguish
			between various types of furniture construction and their appropriate applications, and
			how to use various woodworking machines and power tools for cutting and shaping wood.
			Cabinetmaking courses cover the different methods of joining pieces of wood, how to use
			mechanical fasteners, and how to attach hardware. Initial topics may resemble those
			taught in Woodworking courses; more advanced topics may include how to install plastic
			laminates on surfaces and how to apply spray finishes.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164200"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Cabinetmaking" ;
  skos:definition """Cabinetmaking courses provide students with experience in constructing
			cases, cabinets, counters, and other interior woodwork. Students learn to distinguish
			between various types of furniture construction and their appropriate applications, and
			how to use various woodworking machines and power tools for cutting and shaping wood.
			Cabinetmaking courses cover the different methods of joining pieces of wood, how to use
			mechanical fasteners, and how to attach hardware. Initial topics may resemble those
			taught in Woodworking courses; more advanced topics may include how to install plastic
			laminates on surfaces and how to apply spray finishes.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17007" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Cabinetmaking" .

ceds:NI001517164201
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Masonry courses enable students to learn to construct interior and exterior
			walls, columns, doorways, window openings, fireplaces, chimneys, and foundations from
			brick and concrete block. Along with other activities, students may mix and spread
			cement and mortar, read blueprints and plans, and estimate materials needed for a
			project. Other topics may also include how to layout buildings on footings and how to
			establish grades using a surveying transit.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164201"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Masonry" ;
  skos:definition """Masonry courses enable students to learn to construct interior and exterior
			walls, columns, doorways, window openings, fireplaces, chimneys, and foundations from
			brick and concrete block. Along with other activities, students may mix and spread
			cement and mortar, read blueprints and plans, and estimate materials needed for a
			project. Other topics may also include how to layout buildings on footings and how to
			establish grades using a surveying transit.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17008" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Masonry" .

ceds:NI001517164202
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Formerly known as Building Maintenance, Building Repair and Maintenance
			courses train students to maintain commercial, industrial, and residential buildings and
			homes. Instruction is provided in the basic maintenance and repair of air conditioning,
			heating, plumbing, electrical, and other mechanical systems. Topics covered may include
			identifying and using hand and power tools safely; installing and repairing floor
			coverings, walls, and ceilings; installing and repairing doors, windows, screens, and
			cabinets; applying finishes to prepared surfaces; and repairing roofs, masonry,
			plumbing, and electrical systems.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164202"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Building Repair and Maintenance" ;
  skos:definition """Formerly known as Building Maintenance, Building Repair and Maintenance
			courses train students to maintain commercial, industrial, and residential buildings and
			homes. Instruction is provided in the basic maintenance and repair of air conditioning,
			heating, plumbing, electrical, and other mechanical systems. Topics covered may include
			identifying and using hand and power tools safely; installing and repairing floor
			coverings, walls, and ceilings; installing and repairing doors, windows, screens, and
			cabinets; applying finishes to prepared surfaces; and repairing roofs, masonry,
			plumbing, and electrical systems.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17009" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Building Repair and Maintenance" .

ceds:NI001517164203
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Home Maintenance courses provide students with knowledge and skills related
			to devices and systems found in the home. Course content may include electrical wiring,
			plumbing, window and door repair and installation, wall and floor repair and finishing,
			furniture repair and finishing, and small appliance repair.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164203"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Home Maintenance" ;
  skos:definition """Home Maintenance courses provide students with knowledge and skills related
			to devices and systems found in the home. Course content may include electrical wiring,
			plumbing, window and door repair and installation, wall and floor repair and finishing,
			furniture repair and finishing, and small appliance repair.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17010" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Home Maintenance" .

ceds:NI001517164204
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Wall Finishings courses prepare students to finish exterior or interior
			surfaces by applying protective coating materials such as paint, lacquer, wallpaper,
			plaster, or stucco. Course topics may include instruction in making, mixing, and
			matching paint colors; applying coating with various types of equipment; applying
			wallpaper; lathing, preparing surfaces, smoothing, and finishing.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164204"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Wall Finishings" ;
  skos:definition """Wall Finishings courses prepare students to finish exterior or interior
			surfaces by applying protective coating materials such as paint, lacquer, wallpaper,
			plaster, or stucco. Course topics may include instruction in making, mixing, and
			matching paint colors; applying coating with various types of equipment; applying
			wallpaper; lathing, preparing surfaces, smoothing, and finishing.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17011" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Wall Finishings" .

ceds:NI001517164205
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Upholstering courses prepare students in all aspects of upholstering
			furniture. Topics covered may include installing, repairing, arranging, and securing the
			springs, filler, padding and cover materials of chairs, couches and mattresses; cutting,
			sewing and trimming; cushion filling, tufting, and buttoning; and wood refinishing.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164205"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Upholstering" ;
  skos:definition """Upholstering courses prepare students in all aspects of upholstering
			furniture. Topics covered may include installing, repairing, arranging, and securing the
			springs, filler, padding and cover materials of chairs, couches and mattresses; cutting,
			sewing and trimming; cushion filling, tufting, and buttoning; and wood refinishing.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17012" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Upholstering" .

ceds:NI001517164206
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Commercial Construction courses focus on residential construction principles
			and their relationship to commercial applications. Topics typically covered include
			commercial concrete forming, reinforcement and placement methods, stair construction,
			metal framing, interior finishes, suspended ceiling systems, metal framing and drywall
			applications, and commercial roofing methods and systems. These courses may also address
			equipment and tool usage in commercial construction.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164206"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Commercial Construction" ;
  skos:definition """Commercial Construction courses focus on residential construction
			principles and their relationship to commercial applications. Topics typically covered
			include commercial concrete forming, reinforcement and placement methods, stair
			construction, metal framing, interior finishes, suspended ceiling systems, metal framing
			and drywall applications, and commercial roofing methods and systems. These courses may
			also address equipment and tool usage in commercial construction.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17013" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Commercial Construction" .

ceds:NI001517164207
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Concrete Foundations courses cover concrete and its relationship to
			construction and concrete safety and testing techniques.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164207"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Concrete Foundations" ;
  skos:definition """Concrete Foundations courses cover concrete and its relationship to
			construction and concrete safety and testing techniques.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
