ceds:NI001517164532
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Pre-Engineering Technology courses integrate technology-oriented
			applications of mathematics and science into pre-engineering activities for students.
			Course topics may include material sciences, technology processes, enterprises, and
			career opportunities.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164532"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Pre-Engineering Technology" ;
  skos:definition """Pre-Engineering Technology courses integrate technology-oriented
			applications of mathematics and science into pre-engineering activities for students.
			Course topics may include material sciences, technology processes, enterprises, and
			career opportunities.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21001" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Pre-Engineering Technology" .

ceds:NI001517164533
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Engineering Applications courses provide students with an overview of the
			practical uses of a variety of engineering applications. Topics covered usually include
			hydraulics, pneumatics, computer interfacing, robotics, computer-aided design, computer
			numerical control, and electronics.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164533"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Engineering Applications" ;
  skos:definition """Engineering Applications courses provide students with an overview of the
			practical uses of a variety of engineering applications. Topics covered usually include
			hydraulics, pneumatics, computer interfacing, robotics, computer-aided design, computer
			numerical control, and electronics.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21002" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Engineering Applications" .

ceds:NI001517164534
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Engineering Technology courses provide students with the opportunity to
			focus on one or more areas of industrial technology. Students apply technological
			processes to solve real engineering problems; develop the knowledge and skills to
			design, modify, use, and apply technology; and may also design and build prototypes and
			working models. Topics covered in the course include the nature of technology, use of
			technology, and design processes.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164534"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Engineering Technology" ;
  skos:definition """Engineering Technology courses provide students with the opportunity to
			focus on one or more areas of industrial technology. Students apply technological
			processes to solve real engineering problems; develop the knowledge and skills to
			design, modify, use, and apply technology; and may also design and build prototypes and
			working models. Topics covered in the course include the nature of technology, use of
			technology, and design processes.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21003" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Engineering Technology" .

ceds:NI001517164535
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Principles of Engineering courses provide students with an understanding of
			the engineering/technology field. Students typically explore how engineers use various
			technology systems and manufacturing processes to solve problems; they may also gain an
			appreciation of the social and political consequences of technological change.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164535"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Principles of Engineering" ;
  skos:definition """Principles of Engineering courses provide students with an understanding of
			the engineering/technology field. Students typically explore how engineers use various
			technology systems and manufacturing processes to solve problems; they may also gain an
			appreciation of the social and political consequences of technological change.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21004" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Principles of Engineering" .

ceds:NI001517164536
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Engineering—Comprehensive courses introduce students to and expand their
			knowledge of major engineering concepts such as modeling, systems, design, optimization,
			technology-society interaction, and ethics. Particular topics often include applied
			engineering graphic systems, communicating technical information, engineering design
			principles, material science, research and development processes, and manufacturing
			techniques and systems. The courses may also cover the opportunities and challenges in
			various branches of engineering.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164536"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Engineering—Comprehensive" ;
  skos:definition """Engineering—Comprehensive courses introduce students to and expand their
			knowledge of major engineering concepts such as modeling, systems, design, optimization,
			technology-society interaction, and ethics. Particular topics often include applied
			engineering graphic systems, communicating technical information, engineering design
			principles, material science, research and development processes, and manufacturing
			techniques and systems. The courses may also cover the opportunities and challenges in
			various branches of engineering.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21005" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Engineering—Comprehensive" .

ceds:NI001517164537
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Engineering Design courses offer students experience in solving problems by
			applying a design development process. Often using solid modeling computer design
			software, students develop, analyze, and test product solutions models as well as
			communicate the features of those models.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164537"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Engineering Design" ;
  skos:definition """Engineering Design courses offer students experience in solving problems by
			applying a design development process. Often using solid modeling computer design
			software, students develop, analyze, and test product solutions models as well as
			communicate the features of those models.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21006" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Engineering Design" .

ceds:NI001517164538
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Engineering Design and Development courses provide students with the
			opportunity to apply engineering research principles as they design and construct a
			solution to an engineering problem. Students typically develop and test solutions using
			computer simulations or models but eventually create a working prototype as part of the
			design solution.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164538"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Engineering Design and Development" ;
  skos:definition """Engineering Design and Development courses provide students with the
			opportunity to apply engineering research principles as they design and construct a
			solution to an engineering problem. Students typically develop and test solutions using
			computer simulations or models but eventually create a working prototype as part of the
			design solution.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "21007" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Engineering Design and Development" .

ceds:NI001517164539
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Mechatronics courses provide students with instruction and experience in
			mechatronics, a multidisciplinary subject involving mechanics, electronics, control
			theory, and computer science to design and manufacture products. Mechatronic systems
			form the foundation of robotics, automation, and advanced manufacturing (such as 3D
			printing). These courses typically expose students to the theoretical basis of
			mechatronics in addition to applying these theories to hands-on projects""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164539"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Mechatronics" ;
  skos:definition """Mechatronics courses provide students with instruction and experience in
			mechatronics, a multidisciplinary subject involving mechanics, electronics, control
			theory, and computer science to design and manufacture products. Mechatronic systems
			form the foundation of robotics, automation, and advanced manufacturing (such as 3D
			printing). These courses typically expose students to the theoretical basis of
			mechatronics in addition to applying these theories to hands-on projects""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "13104" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Mechatronics" .

ceds:NI001517164540
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Quantitative Reasoning courses allow students to apply basic mathematical
			skills and analytical concepts to real-world situations. These courses focus on
			strategies required for problem solving, critical evaluation of numerical information,
			decision making, and economic productivity in real-world applications. Topics may
			include numeracy, ratio and proportional reasoning, modeling, financial literacy,
			validity studies (logic and set theory), and statistics.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164540"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Quantitative Reasoning" ;
  skos:definition """Quantitative Reasoning courses allow students to apply basic mathematical
			skills and analytical concepts to real-world situations. These courses focus on
			strategies required for problem solving, critical evaluation of numerical information,
			decision making, and economic productivity in real-world applications. Topics may
			include numeracy, ratio and proportional reasoning, modeling, financial literacy,
			validity studies (logic and set theory), and statistics.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "02158" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Quantitative Reasoning" .

ceds:NI001517164541
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level precalculus courses, AP Precalculus courses introduce students to mathematical modeling and functions that serve as a foundation for calculus and other college-level mathematics needed for a variety of STEM majors and careers. Topics typically include polynomial and rational functions, exponential and logarithmic functions, trigonometric and polar functions, and functions involving parameters, vectors, and matrices." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164541"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Precalculus" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level precalculus courses, AP Precalculus courses introduce students to mathematical modeling and functions that serve as a foundation for calculus and other college-level mathematics needed for a variety of STEM majors and careers. Topics typically include polynomial and rational functions, exponential and logarithmic functions, trigonometric and polar functions, and functions involving parameters, vectors, and matrices." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "02114" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Precalculus" .

ceds:NI001517164542
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level English courses, AP Seminar: English courses expose students to a variety of texts covering multiple genres, topics, and rhetorical contexts in a seminar-style setting. These courses foster students' ability to summarize and explain the salient ideas in a text by analyzing an author's perspective, rhetorical choices, and argumentative structure. Students evaluate a variety of literary, informational, and visual texts, and synthesize perspectives to develop evidence-based arguments. Students convey their findings through multiple written formats, multimedia presentations, and oral defenses." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164542"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "AP Seminar: English" ;
  skos:definition "Following the College Board's suggested curriculum designed to parallel college-level English courses, AP Seminar: English courses expose students to a variety of texts covering multiple genres, topics, and rhetorical contexts in a seminar-style setting. These courses foster students' ability to summarize and explain the salient ideas in a text by analyzing an author's perspective, rhetorical choices, and argumentative structure. Students evaluate a variety of literary, informational, and visual texts, and synthesize perspectives to develop evidence-based arguments. Students convey their findings through multiple written formats, multimedia presentations, and oral defenses." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "01013" ;
  skos:prefLabel "AP Seminar: English" .

ceds:NI001517164543
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Cambridge International (CI) English General Paper courses prepare students
			to take the Cambridge English General Paper assessments. These courses teach students to
			write in English through the study of a wide range of contemporary topics, to analyze
			opinions and ideas, and to construct arguments. Students will gain the skill of English
			writing comprehension as well as skills of developing arguments, independent reasoning,
			interpretation, persuasion, and presenting a clear point of view.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164543"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "CI English General Paper" ;
  skos:definition """Cambridge International (CI) English General Paper courses prepare students
			to take the Cambridge English General Paper assessments. These courses teach students to
			write in English through the study of a wide range of contemporary topics, to analyze
			opinions and ideas, and to construct arguments. Students will gain the skill of English
			writing comprehension as well as skills of developing arguments, independent reasoning,
			interpretation, persuasion, and presenting a clear point of view.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "01106" ;
  skos:prefLabel "CI English General Paper" .

ceds:NI001517164544
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Cambridge International (CI) English Language courses prepare students to
			take the Cambridge English Language assessments. These courses teach students to
			critically respond to a variety of texts in a range of forms, styles, and contexts, and
			promote skills of communication, reading, research, and analysis. Students will gain an
			understanding of English language features and issues as well as develop writing skills
			for different purposes and audiences.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164544"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "CI English Language" ;
  skos:definition """Cambridge International (CI) English Language courses prepare students to
			take the Cambridge English Language assessments. These courses teach students to
			critically respond to a variety of texts in a range of forms, styles, and contexts, and
			promote skills of communication, reading, research, and analysis. Students will gain an
			understanding of English language features and issues as well as develop writing skills
			for different purposes and audiences.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "01014" ;
  skos:prefLabel "CI English Language" .

ceds:NI001517164545
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Cambridge International (CI) English Literature courses prepare students to
			take the Cambridge English Literature assessments. These courses teach students the
			three main forms of literature; prose, poetry, and drama, through texts from a wide
			range of different periods and cultures. Students will learn to read, analyze, and
			discuss the critical context of literature as well as develop skills of effective and
			appropriate communication.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164545"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "CI English Literature" ;
  skos:definition """Cambridge International (CI) English Literature courses prepare students to
			take the Cambridge English Literature assessments. These courses teach students the
			three main forms of literature; prose, poetry, and drama, through texts from a wide
			range of different periods and cultures. Students will learn to read, analyze, and
			discuss the critical context of literature as well as develop skills of effective and
			appropriate communication.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "01070" ;
  skos:prefLabel "CI English Literature" .

