			calculation predictions. Specific content depends upon state standards for grade 1.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "02031" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Mathematics (grade 1)" .

ceds:NI001517163265
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Mathematics (grade 2) courses typically continue to build a conceptual
			foundation in number, operation, and quantitative reasoning; patterns, relationships,
			and algebraic thinking; geometry and spatial reasoning; and measurement. Students begin
			to incorporate the context of time and money. These courses often require students to
			develop their numerical fluency, particularly in addition and subtraction, and to solve
			problems using those operations as well as estimation. Specific content depends upon
			state standards for grade 2.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163265"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Mathematics (grade 2)" ;
  skos:definition """Mathematics (grade 2) courses typically continue to build a conceptual
			foundation in number, operation, and quantitative reasoning; patterns, relationships,
			and algebraic thinking; geometry and spatial reasoning; and measurement. Students begin
			to incorporate the context of time and money. These courses often require students to
			develop their numerical fluency, particularly in addition and subtraction, and to solve
			problems using those operations as well as estimation. Specific content depends upon
			state standards for grade 2.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "02032" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Mathematics (grade 2)" .

ceds:NI001517163571
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Dance (grade 5) courses typically provide activities that foster creative
			expression, communication through artistic endeavor, appreciation of culture and
			heritage, and evaluative and critical thinking using the art of dance. Activities may
			include those that enable students to develop their technique, learn different styles of
			dance, appreciate the culture and history of dance forms, and strengthen the ability to
			discern and critique. Specific course content conforms to any existing state standards
			for grade 5.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163571"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Dance (grade 5)" ;
  skos:definition """Dance (grade 5) courses typically provide activities that foster creative
			expression, communication through artistic endeavor, appreciation of culture and
			heritage, and evaluative and critical thinking using the art of dance. Activities may
			include those that enable students to develop their technique, learn different styles of
			dance, appreciate the culture and history of dance forms, and strengthen the ability to
			discern and critique. Specific course content conforms to any existing state standards
			for grade 5.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05035" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Dance (grade 5)" .

ceds:NI001517163572
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Dance—General courses involve content that is not grade differentiated and
			may apply to a range of consecutive grades (e.g., "by third grade, students should know
			and be able to do…"). These courses include content that may be applicable to states or
			localities that do not employ grade-level content standards. [These courses provide
			broad content that is not organized as described elsewhere (i.e., Dance, early childhood
			education through grade 8).]""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163572"^^xsd:token ;
