ceds:NI001517163579
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Introduction to Theater courses provide an overview of the art, conventions,
			and history of the theater arts. Although the courses sometimes include experiential
			exercises, they emphasize learning about theater processes rather than theatrical
			production and performance. Course topics include one or more of the following: basic
			techniques in acting, major developments in dramatic literature, major playwrights, the
			evolution of theater as a cultural tradition, and critical appreciation of the art and
			craft of the theater profession.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163579"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Introduction to Theater" ;
  skos:definition """Introduction to Theater courses provide an overview of the art,
			conventions, and history of the theater arts. Although the courses sometimes include
			experiential exercises, they emphasize learning about theater processes rather than
			theatrical production and performance. Course topics include one or more of the
			following: basic techniques in acting, major developments in dramatic literature, major
			playwrights, the evolution of theater as a cultural tradition, and critical appreciation
			of the art and craft of the theater profession.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05051" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Introduction to Theater" .

ceds:NI001517163580
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Theater Arts courses focus on the study and performance of drama in its many forms, including musical theater, drama, and comedy. These courses review a wide range of scripted materials (such as plays, screenplays, teleplays, readers' theater scripts); dramatic criticism; techniques for creating original dramatic works; and the role of dramatic arts in society. Theater Arts courses typically require students to perform collaboratively, be involved in the critique of dramatic works, and learn methods for self-expression." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163580"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Theater Arts" ;
  skos:definition "Theater Arts courses focus on the study and performance of drama in its many forms, including musical theater, drama, and comedy. These courses review a wide range of scripted materials (such as plays, screenplays, teleplays, readers' theater scripts); dramatic criticism; techniques for creating original dramatic works; and the role of dramatic arts in society. Theater Arts courses typically require students to perform collaboratively, be involved in the critique of dramatic works, and learn methods for self-expression." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05052" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Theater Arts" .

ceds:NI001517163581
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Theater—Comprehensive courses help students experience and develop skill in one or more aspects of theatrical production. Introductory courses provide an overview of theatrical elements including acting, set design, stage management, directing, playwriting, and production. Advanced courses concentrate on extending and refining dramatic technique, expanding students' exposure to different types of theatrical styles, genres, and traditions, and increasing their participation in public productions." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163581"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Theater—Comprehensive" ;
  skos:definition "Theater—Comprehensive courses help students experience and develop skill in one or more aspects of theatrical production. Introductory courses provide an overview of theatrical elements including acting, set design, stage management, directing, playwriting, and production. Advanced courses concentrate on extending and refining dramatic technique, expanding students' exposure to different types of theatrical styles, genres, and traditions, and increasing their participation in public productions." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05053" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Theater—Comprehensive" .

ceds:NI001517163582
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Theater—Acting/Performance courses provide students with experience and skill development in one or more aspects of theatrical production, by concentrating on acting and performance skills. Introductory courses explore fundamental techniques, while advanced courses extend and refine technique, expand students' exposure to different types of theatrical craft and traditions from varied social and historical contexts, and increase their participation in public productions." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163582"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Theater—Acting/Performance" ;
  skos:definition "Theater—Acting/Performance courses provide students with experience and skill development in one or more aspects of theatrical production, by concentrating on acting and performance skills. Introductory courses explore fundamental techniques, while advanced courses extend and refine technique, expand students' exposure to different types of theatrical craft and traditions from varied social and historical contexts, and increase their participation in public productions." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05055" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Theater—Acting/Performance" .

ceds:NI001517163583
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Theater—Stagecraft courses provide students with an understanding of the
			various aspects of theatrical production, including lighting, costuming, sound, set
			construction, makeup, stage management, and the use of computer and media-based
			applications. These courses prepare students to engage in the hands-on application of
			these production elements in design and technology courses.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163583"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Theater—Stagecraft" ;
  skos:definition """Theater—Stagecraft courses provide students with an understanding of the
			various aspects of theatrical production, including lighting, costuming, sound, set
			construction, makeup, stage management, and the use of computer and media-based
			applications. These courses prepare students to engage in the hands-on application of
			these production elements in design and technology courses.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05056" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Theater—Stagecraft" .

ceds:NI001517163584
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Theater—Directing courses focus on developing students' skills in translating a script into a final production. Directing courses enable each student to create an artistic vision and develop a personal aesthetic. These courses may expose students to different types of theatrical techniques and traditions. They also provide students with opportunities to direct the performances of others (either in scenes or in a full production)." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163584"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Theater—Directing" ;
  skos:definition "Theater—Directing courses focus on developing students' skills in translating a script into a final production. Directing courses enable each student to create an artistic vision and develop a personal aesthetic. These courses may expose students to different types of theatrical techniques and traditions. They also provide students with opportunities to direct the performances of others (either in scenes or in a full production)." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05057" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Theater—Directing" .

ceds:NI001517163589
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """IB Theatre courses prepare students to take the International Baccalaureate
			(IB) Theatre exams. IB Theatre courses encourage students to examine the theory,
			history, and culture of theatre. These courses also help students develop the
			organizational and technical skills to express themselves through scripted performance,
			workshops, and independent project(s).""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163589"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "IB Theatre" ;
  skos:definition """IB Theatre courses prepare students to take the International Baccalaureate
			(IB) Theatre exams. IB Theatre courses encourage students to examine the theory,
			history, and culture of theatre. These courses also help students develop the
			organizational and technical skills to express themselves through scripted performance,
			workshops, and independent project(s).""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05062" ;
  skos:prefLabel "IB Theatre" .

ceds:NI001517163585
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Formerly known as Playwriting, Playwriting and Screenwriting courses help students understand and employ writing principles and techniques to create original scripts suitable for theater, film, and/or television production. These courses explore the appropriate techniques of each genre and develop a personal voice, style, and aesthetic by examining the work of various playwrights and screenwriters. Students may examine the creative writing craft, scene writing, script development, stage and/or camera instructions, line and moment analysis, script reading, script editing, and the creation of a production." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163585"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Playwriting and Screenwriting" ;
  skos:definition "Formerly known as Playwriting, Playwriting and Screenwriting courses help students understand and employ writing principles and techniques to create original scripts suitable for theater, film, and/or television production. These courses explore the appropriate techniques of each genre and develop a personal voice, style, and aesthetic by examining the work of various playwrights and screenwriters. Students may examine the creative writing craft, scene writing, script development, stage and/or camera instructions, line and moment analysis, script reading, script editing, and the creation of a production." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05058" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Playwriting and Screenwriting" .

ceds:NI001517163586
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """History and Literature of the Theatre courses explore in depth the
			structure, elements, and style of dramatic compositions, and, as an extension, how the
			dramatic literature influenced theatrical production and acting styles throughout
			history. Some courses may focus more on the literature component than on the theatre
			(with increased emphasis on critique and analysis), but most courses connect these
			subjects, exploring their interrelationship. Major contributors (i.e. playwrights,
			directors, designers) and the architecture of the theater may also be included as topics
			of study.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163586"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "History and Literature of the Theater" ;
  skos:definition """History and Literature of the Theatre courses explore in depth the
			structure, elements, and style of dramatic compositions, and, as an extension, how the
			dramatic literature influenced theatrical production and acting styles throughout
			history. Some courses may focus more on the literature component than on the theatre
			(with increased emphasis on critique and analysis), but most courses connect these
			subjects, exploring their interrelationship. Major contributors (i.e. playwrights,
			directors, designers) and the architecture of the theater may also be included as topics
			of study.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05059" ;
  skos:prefLabel "History and Literature of the Theater" .

ceds:NI001517163587
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Musical Theater courses provide students with the opportunity to explore
			and/or participate in various aspects of musical theater, including auditioning,
			singing, acting, and dancing. These courses review the history and evolution of musical
			theatre, its literature and artists, and styles of composition and vocal presentation.
			Students work collaboratively on performances, including solo, duet, and ensemble work.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163587"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Musical Theater" ;
  skos:definition """Musical Theater courses provide students with the opportunity to explore
			and/or participate in various aspects of musical theater, including auditioning,
			singing, acting, and dancing. These courses review the history and evolution of musical
			theatre, its literature and artists, and styles of composition and vocal presentation.
			Students work collaboratively on performances, including solo, duet, and ensemble work.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05060" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Musical Theater" .

ceds:NI001517163588
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Theatrical Production and Management courses prepare students to manage the planning, design, preparation, and production of plays and other theatrical performances. Course content may include instruction in theatrical design, program management, dramatic production, rehearsal management, personnel management and casting, actor coaching, directing concepts and techniques, dramaturgy, script interpretation, business management, marketing, public relations, and communications skills." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163588"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Theatrical Production and Management" ;
  skos:definition "Theatrical Production and Management courses prepare students to manage the planning, design, preparation, and production of plays and other theatrical performances. Course content may include instruction in theatrical design, program management, dramatic production, rehearsal management, personnel management and casting, actor coaching, directing concepts and techniques, dramaturgy, script interpretation, business management, marketing, public relations, and communications skills." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05061" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Theatrical Production and Management" .

ceds:NI001517163590
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Drama (grade 1) courses enable students to express themselves through
			dramatic play and storytelling. Course content typically includes the use of movement,
			language, character, plot, and spectacle to portray imaginary or real experiences.
			Specific course content conforms to any existing state standards for grade 1.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163590"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Drama (grade 1)" ;
  skos:definition """Drama (grade 1) courses enable students to express themselves through
			dramatic play and storytelling. Course content typically includes the use of movement,
			language, character, plot, and spectacle to portray imaginary or real experiences.
			Specific course content conforms to any existing state standards for grade 1.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05071" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Drama (grade 1)" .

ceds:NI001517163591
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Orchestra courses help develop students' technique for playing strings along with woodwind, brass, and percussion instruments. These courses may emphasize collaboration through rehearsal and performance experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163591"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Orchestra" ;
  skos:definition "Orchestra courses help develop students' technique for playing strings along with woodwind, brass, and percussion instruments. These courses may emphasize collaboration through rehearsal and performance experiences in creating and responding to music." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05104" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Orchestra" .

ceds:NI001517163592
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Formerly known as Contemporary Band, Contemporary Instrumental Ensemble courses help students perform a variety of contemporary styles, such as traditional jazz, jazz improvisation, and rock. At the same time, these courses cultivate students' technique on instruments appropriate to the style(s) performed—brass, woodwind, string, percussion instruments, and/or electronic. These ensembles emphasize instrumental music but may also include vocal music. Advanced coursework provides students with opportunities for growth through rehearsal and performance, improvisation, or creating and performing their own compositions." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163592"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Contemporary Instrumental Ensemble" ;
  skos:definition "Formerly known as Contemporary Band, Contemporary Instrumental Ensemble courses help students perform a variety of contemporary styles, such as traditional jazz, jazz improvisation, and rock. At the same time, these courses cultivate students' technique on instruments appropriate to the style(s) performed—brass, woodwind, string, percussion instruments, and/or electronic. These ensembles emphasize instrumental music but may also include vocal music. Advanced coursework provides students with opportunities for growth through rehearsal and performance, improvisation, or creating and performing their own compositions." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05105" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Contemporary Instrumental Ensemble" .

ceds:NI001517163593
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Formerly known as Instrumental Ensemble, Small Ensemble courses help students perform a variety of musical styles (e.g., traditional chamber music, jazz, and rock). At the same time, these courses help cultivate students' technique on instruments appropriate to the style(s) performed—brass, woodwind, string, percussion instruments, and/or electronic and provide experiences in creating and responding to music. Courses typically range in size from 2 to 20 performers." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163593"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Small Ensemble" ;
  skos:definition "Formerly known as Instrumental Ensemble, Small Ensemble courses help students perform a variety of musical styles (e.g., traditional chamber music, jazz, and rock). At the same time, these courses help cultivate students' technique on instruments appropriate to the style(s) performed—brass, woodwind, string, percussion instruments, and/or electronic and provide experiences in creating and responding to music. Courses typically range in size from 2 to 20 performers." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05106" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Small Ensemble" .

ceds:NI001517163594
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Piano courses provide students an introduction to, and refine the
			fundamentals of, music and keyboard including literature and techniques such as scales,
			chords, and melodic lines and may offer instruction in more advanced techniques. Formal
			and informal performances are typically included as well as experiences in creating and
			responding to music.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163594"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Piano" ;
  skos:definition """Piano courses provide students an introduction to, and refine the
			fundamentals of, music and keyboard including literature and techniques such as scales,
			chords, and melodic lines and may offer instruction in more advanced techniques. Formal
			and informal performances are typically included as well as experiences in creating and
			responding to music.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "05107" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Piano" .

