ceds:NI001517163902
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Journalism courses (typically associated with the production of a school newspaper, yearbook, or literary magazine) emphasize writing style and technique as well as production values and organization. Journalism courses introduce students to the concepts of newsworthiness and press responsibility; develop students' skills in writing and editing stories, headlines, and captions; and teach students the principles of production design, layout, and printing. Photography, photojournalism, and digital technology skills may be included." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163902"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Journalism" ;
  skos:definition "Journalism courses (typically associated with the production of a school newspaper, yearbook, or literary magazine) emphasize writing style and technique as well as production values and organization. Journalism courses introduce students to the concepts of newsworthiness and press responsibility; develop students' skills in writing and editing stories, headlines, and captions; and teach students the principles of production design, layout, and printing. Photography, photojournalism, and digital technology skills may be included." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "11101" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Journalism" .

ceds:NI001517163903
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Photojournalism courses expose students to the manner in which photography
			is used to convey information and experiences. Typically coordinated with production of
			the school newspaper, yearbook, or other media product, photojournalism courses provide
			students with the opportunity to improve their photo composition and digital technology
			skills, and to apply their art to journalistic endeavors. These courses may also cover
			film development.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517163903"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Photojournalism" ;
  skos:definition """Photojournalism courses expose students to the manner in which photography
			is used to convey information and experiences. Typically coordinated with production of
