ceds:NI001517164229
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Exploration of Electricity/Electronics courses offer instruction in the theory of electricity and in the terminology, skills, and safety procedures common to careers involving electricity and electronics. Topics include (but are not limited to) Ohm's law, electrical equipment, wire systems, and so on; career exploration is often (but not always) an integral part of these courses." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164229"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Exploration of Electricity/Electronics" ;
  skos:definition "Exploration of Electricity/Electronics courses offer instruction in the theory of electricity and in the terminology, skills, and safety procedures common to careers involving electricity and electronics. Topics include (but are not limited to) Ohm's law, electrical equipment, wire systems, and so on; career exploration is often (but not always) an integral part of these courses." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17101" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Exploration of Electricity/Electronics" .

ceds:NI001517164230
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Electricity—Comprehensive courses provide a survey of the theory,
			terminology, equipment, and practical experience in the skills needed for careers in the
			electrical field. These courses typically include AC and DC circuitry, safety, and the
			National Electrical Code and may cover such skills as those involved in building
			circuits; wiring residential, commercial, and/or industrial buildings; installing
			lighting, power circuits, and cables; and estimating job costs. As students progress,
			their projects become more complex and expansive. In these courses, safety is stressed,
			and a career exploration component may be offered.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164230"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Electricity—Comprehensive" ;
  skos:definition """Electricity—Comprehensive courses provide a survey of the theory,
			terminology, equipment, and practical experience in the skills needed for careers in the
			electrical field. These courses typically include AC and DC circuitry, safety, and the
			National Electrical Code and may cover such skills as those involved in building
			circuits; wiring residential, commercial, and/or industrial buildings; installing
			lighting, power circuits, and cables; and estimating job costs. As students progress,
			their projects become more complex and expansive. In these courses, safety is stressed,
			and a career exploration component may be offered.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17102" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Electricity—Comprehensive" .

ceds:NI001517164231
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Covering many of the same topics as Electricity—Comprehensive courses,
			Residential Wiring courses apply the knowledge and skills that students acquire to the
			electrical systems found in family dwellings. Because these courses emphasize
			residential electricity, topics may also include cable installation, telephone systems,
			and the installation of lighting fixtures, outlets, and so on. Maintenance and repair
			skills are often included as course topics.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164231"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Residential Wiring" ;
  skos:definition """Covering many of the same topics as Electricity—Comprehensive courses,
			Residential Wiring courses apply the knowledge and skills that students acquire to the
			electrical systems found in family dwellings. Because these courses emphasize
			residential electricity, topics may also include cable installation, telephone systems,
			and the installation of lighting fixtures, outlets, and so on. Maintenance and repair
			skills are often included as course topics.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17103" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Residential Wiring" .

ceds:NI001517164232
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Covering many of the same topics as Electricity—Comprehensive courses,
			Industrial Electricity courses apply the knowledge and skills that students acquire to
			the electrical systems used in industry. Because of this emphasis, these courses may
			also cover the installation of transformers and control devices, emergency generator
			systems, and other industrial applications.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164232"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Industrial Electricity" ;
  skos:definition """Covering many of the same topics as Electricity—Comprehensive courses,
			Industrial Electricity courses apply the knowledge and skills that students acquire to
			the electrical systems used in industry. Because of this emphasis, these courses may
			also cover the installation of transformers and control devices, emergency generator
			systems, and other industrial applications.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17104" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Industrial Electricity" .

ceds:NI001517164233
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses provide students with specialized knowledge and help them
			develop skills in particular topics concerning the nature, behavior, and application of
			electrical current.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164233"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Electricity" ;
  skos:definition """These courses provide students with specialized knowledge and help them
			develop skills in particular topics concerning the nature, behavior, and application of
			electrical current.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17105" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Electricity" .

ceds:NI001517164234
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Electronics—Comprehensive courses provide a survey of the theory,
			terminology, equipment, and practical experience in the skills needed for careers in the
			electronic field as well as typically cover the theory of electricity. Course topics may
			include AC, DC, analog, and integrated circuitry and solid state and digital devices,
			amplifiers, and semiconductors. Skills covered may involve the repair, maintenance, and
			building of electronic equipment such as radios, television sets, and industrial
			equipment.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164234"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Electronics—Comprehensive" ;
  skos:definition """Electronics—Comprehensive courses provide a survey of the theory,
			terminology, equipment, and practical experience in the skills needed for careers in the
			electronic field as well as typically cover the theory of electricity. Course topics may
			include AC, DC, analog, and integrated circuitry and solid state and digital devices,
			amplifiers, and semiconductors. Skills covered may involve the repair, maintenance, and
			building of electronic equipment such as radios, television sets, and industrial
			equipment.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17106" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Electronics—Comprehensive" .

ceds:NI001517164235
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Individual courses in this category offer specialized training in topics
			related to electronics such as diodes, transistors, digital techniques, solid-state
			devices, analog circuits, and microprocessors.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164235"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Electronics" ;
  skos:definition """Individual courses in this category offer specialized training in topics
			related to electronics such as diodes, transistors, digital techniques, solid-state
			devices, analog circuits, and microprocessors.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17107" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Electronics" .

ceds:NI001517164236
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Electricity/Electronics—General courses teach fundamental concepts of
			electricity and electronics, including safety procedures, and may introduce students to
			the available occupations in electrical and electronic industries. Topics covered
			typically include components of circuits; reading schematics and diagrams; electricity
			and electronics as sources of energy; signal transmission; and using equipment common to
			these occupations, such as ammeters, voltmeters, capacitor checkers, transistor testers,
			signal generators, and ohmmeters.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164236"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Electricity/Electronics—General" ;
  skos:definition """Electricity/Electronics—General courses teach fundamental concepts of
			electricity and electronics, including safety procedures, and may introduce students to
			the available occupations in electrical and electronic industries. Topics covered
			typically include components of circuits; reading schematics and diagrams; electricity
			and electronics as sources of energy; signal transmission; and using equipment common to
			these occupations, such as ammeters, voltmeters, capacitor checkers, transistor testers,
			signal generators, and ohmmeters.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17108" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Electricity/Electronics—General" .

ceds:NI001517164237
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """These courses provide instruction in the theory and skills needed in fields
			involving electricity and electronics and related fields that focus on electrical wiring
			or electronic signals.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164237"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Particular Topics in Electricity/Electronics" ;
  skos:definition """These courses provide instruction in the theory and skills needed in fields
			involving electricity and electronics and related fields that focus on electrical wiring
			or electronic signals.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17109" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Particular Topics in Electricity/Electronics" .

ceds:NI001517164238
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """In these courses, analog and digital circuits and systems are compared.
			Topics covered include binary and continuously variable currents and signals (typically
			in the context of voltage), waveforms, signal loss and distortion, modulation, and
			signal processing. These courses may also introduce other media, such as sound waves and
			liquids.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164238"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Analog and Digital Circuits" ;
  skos:definition """In these courses, analog and digital circuits and systems are compared.
			Topics covered include binary and continuously variable currents and signals (typically
			in the context of voltage), waveforms, signal loss and distortion, modulation, and
			signal processing. These courses may also introduce other media, such as sound waves and
			liquids.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17110" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Analog and Digital Circuits" .

ceds:NI001517164239
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Analog Circuit courses emphasize currents and voltages that have
			continuously variable signals and, due to that emphasis, concentrate on signal
			modulation, transmission and reception, signal loss and distortion, and waveforms. These
			courses may also address conversion techniques.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164239"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Analog Circuits" ;
  skos:definition """Analog Circuit courses emphasize currents and voltages that have
			continuously variable signals and, due to that emphasis, concentrate on signal
			modulation, transmission and reception, signal loss and distortion, and waveforms. These
			courses may also address conversion techniques.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17111" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Analog Circuits" .

ceds:NI001517164240
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001517, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Digital Circuit courses emphasize currents and voltages that have binary
			states and, due to that emphasis, concentrate on transmission and reception of binary
			data, signal loss, and processing circuitry. These courses may also address conversion
			techniques.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001517164240"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Digital Circuits" ;
  skos:definition """Digital Circuit courses emphasize currents and voltages that have binary
			states and, due to that emphasis, concentrate on transmission and reception of binary
			data, signal loss, and processing circuitry. These courses may also address conversion
			techniques.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001517 ;
  skos:notation "17112" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Digital Circuits" .

