ceds:NI001874129085
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001874, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Compounds containing hydrogen, fluorine, chlorine, and carbon atoms.
			Although ozone depleting substances, they are less potent at destroying stratospheric
			ozone than chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs). They have been introduced as temporary
			replacements for CFCs and are also greenhouse gases.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001874129085"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Hydrochlorofluorocarbons" ;
  skos:definition """Compounds containing hydrogen, fluorine, chlorine, and carbon atoms.
			Although ozone depleting substances, they are less potent at destroying stratospheric
			ozone than chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs). They have been introduced as temporary
			replacements for CFCs and are also greenhouse gases.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001874 ;
  skos:notation "13664" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Hydrochlorofluorocarbons" .

ceds:NI001874129086
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001874, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Lead is a toxic metal that was used for many years in various products. Lead can affect children's brains and developing nervous systems, causing reduced IQ, learning disabilities, and behavioral problems. Lead is also harmful to adults. Lead in dust is the most common way people are exposed to lead. People can also get lead in their bodies from lead in soil, paint chips and drinking water from lead-containing pipes or plumbing fixtures." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001874129086"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Lead" ;
  skos:definition "Lead is a toxic metal that was used for many years in various products. Lead can affect children's brains and developing nervous systems, causing reduced IQ, learning disabilities, and behavioral problems. Lead is also harmful to adults. Lead in dust is the most common way people are exposed to lead. People can also get lead in their bodies from lead in soil, paint chips and drinking water from lead-containing pipes or plumbing fixtures." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001874 ;
  skos:notation "02899" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Lead" .

ceds:NI001874129087
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001874, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Mercury is a naturally occurring element that is found in air, water and
			soil. Mercury is found in many rocks including coal. When coal is burned, mercury is
			released into the environment. High levels can harm the brain, heart, kidneys, lungs,
			and immune system of people of all ages.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001874129087"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Mercury" ;
  skos:definition """Mercury is a naturally occurring element that is found in air, water and
			soil. Mercury is found in many rocks including coal. When coal is burned, mercury is
			released into the environment. High levels can harm the brain, heart, kidneys, lungs,
			and immune system of people of all ages.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001874 ;
  skos:notation "13665" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Mercury" .

ceds:NI001874129088
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001874, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """A hydrocarbon that is a greenhouse gas with a global warming potential most
			recently estimated at 23 times that of carbon dioxide. Methane is produced through
			anaerobic (without oxygen) decomposition of waste in landfills, animal digestion,
			decomposition of animal wastes, production and distribution of natural gas and
			petroleum, coal production, and incomplete fossil fuel combustion.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001874129088"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Methane" ;
  skos:definition """A hydrocarbon that is a greenhouse gas with a global warming potential most
			recently estimated at 23 times that of carbon dioxide. Methane is produced through
			anaerobic (without oxygen) decomposition of waste in landfills, animal digestion,
			decomposition of animal wastes, production and distribution of natural gas and
			petroleum, coal production, and incomplete fossil fuel combustion.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001874 ;
  skos:notation "13666" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Methane" .

ceds:NI001874129089
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001874, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Molds are part of the natural environment. Outdoors, molds break down dead organic matter such as fallen leaves and dead trees, but indoors, mold growth should be avoided. Molds reproduce by means of tiny spores. Mold may begin growing indoors when mold spores land on surfaces that are wet. Molds have the potential to cause health problems. Molds produce allergens, irritants, and in some cases, potentially toxic substances (mycotoxins). Inhaling or touching mold or mold spores may cause allergic reactions in sensitive individuals." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001874129089"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Mold" ;
  skos:definition "Molds are part of the natural environment. Outdoors, molds break down dead organic matter such as fallen leaves and dead trees, but indoors, mold growth should be avoided. Molds reproduce by means of tiny spores. Mold may begin growing indoors when mold spores land on surfaces that are wet. Molds have the potential to cause health problems. Molds produce allergens, irritants, and in some cases, potentially toxic substances (mycotoxins). Inhaling or touching mold or mold spores may cause allergic reactions in sensitive individuals." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001874 ;
  skos:notation "02900" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Mold" .

ceds:NI001874129090
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001874, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description """Gases consisting of one molecule of nitrogen and varying numbers of oxygen
			molecules. Nitrogen oxides are produced in the emissions of vehicle exhausts and from
			power stations. In the atmosphere, nitrogen oxides can contribute to formation of
			photochemical ozone (smog), can impair visibility and have health consequences, they are
			thus considered plants.""" ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001874129090"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Nitrogen Oxides" ;
  skos:definition """Gases consisting of one molecule of nitrogen and varying numbers of oxygen
			molecules. Nitrogen oxides are produced in the emissions of vehicle exhausts and from
			power stations. In the atmosphere, nitrogen oxides can contribute to formation of
			photochemical ozone (smog), can impair visibility and have health consequences, they are
			thus considered plants.""" ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001874 ;
  skos:notation "13667" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Nitrogen Oxides" .

