  skos:prefLabel "Vapor intrusion" .

ceds:NI001874129102
  a owl:NamedIndividual, ceds:C001874, skos:Concept ;
  dc11:creator "Common Education Data Standards" ;
  dc11:description "Volatile organic compounds (VOCs) are emitted as gases from certain solids or liquids. VOCs include a variety of chemicals, some of which may have short- and long-term adverse health effects. Concentrations of many VOCs are consistently higher indoors (up to ten times higher) than outdoors. VOCs are emitted by a wide array of products numbering in the thousands. Examples include: paints and lacquers, paint strippers, cleaning supplies, pesticides, building materials and furnishings, office equipment such as copiers and printers, correction fluids and carbonless copy paper, graphics and craft materials including glues and adhesives, permanent markers and photographic solutions VOCs can cause eye, nose and throat irritation, headaches, loss of coordination, nausea, damage to liver, kidney and central nervous system." ;
  dc11:identifier "NI001874129102"^^xsd:token ;
  rdfs:label "Volatile organic compounds" ;
  skos:definition "Volatile organic compounds (VOCs) are emitted as gases from certain solids or liquids. VOCs include a variety of chemicals, some of which may have short- and long-term adverse health effects. Concentrations of many VOCs are consistently higher indoors (up to ten times higher) than outdoors. VOCs are emitted by a wide array of products numbering in the thousands. Examples include: paints and lacquers, paint strippers, cleaning supplies, pesticides, building materials and furnishings, office equipment such as copiers and printers, correction fluids and carbonless copy paper, graphics and craft materials including glues and adhesives, permanent markers and photographic solutions VOCs can cause eye, nose and throat irritation, headaches, loss of coordination, nausea, damage to liver, kidney and central nervous system." ;
  skos:inScheme ceds:C001874 ;
  skos:notation "13675" ;
  skos:prefLabel "Volatile organic compounds" .

